<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4 (LSH algorithm guarantee for ANNA). ‣ 3.2 Transformer based on Approximate Nearest Neighbor Attention ‣ 3 Approximate Nearest Neighbor Attention ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a></h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We restate <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4 (LSH algorithm guarantee for ANNA). ‣ 3.2 Transformer based on Approximate Nearest Neighbor Attention ‣ 3 Approximate Nearest Neighbor Attention ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a> here, which gives the theoretical guarantee for <a href="#alg1" title="In 3.2 Transformer based on Approximate Nearest Neighbor Attention ‣ 3 Approximate Nearest Neighbor Attention ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(LSH algorithm guarantee for ANNA; <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4 (LSH algorithm guarantee for ANNA). ‣ 3.2 Transformer based on Approximate Nearest Neighbor Attention ‣ 3 Approximate Nearest Neighbor Attention ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;\sqrt{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;\sqrt{3}</annotation></semantics></math>,
LSH family <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> that is <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r,cr,p_{1},p_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r,cr,p_{1},p_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>-sensitive with quality <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho&lt;1/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho&lt;1/3</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=\Theta(N^{3\rho}\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=\Theta(N^{3\rho}\log N)</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=\Theta(\log_{1/p_{2}}N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=\Theta(\log_{1/p_{2}}N)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <a href="#alg1" title="In 3.2 Transformer based on Approximate Nearest Neighbor Attention ‣ 3 Approximate Nearest Neighbor Attention ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>) implements an ANNA mechanism with parameters <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r,c,\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r,c,\ell</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=\smash{O(1/N^{1-3\rho})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=\smash{O(1/N^{1-3\rho})}</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">2</span></span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              <span id="footnote2.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">Optimal (data-oblivious) LSH schemes achieve </span><math id="footnote2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1/c^{2}+o(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1/c^{2}+o(1)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote2.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Andoni and Indyk (2006)</a></cite><span id="footnote2.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">.
Since we assume </span><math id="footnote2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;\sqrt{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;\sqrt{3}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote2.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">, the failure probability </span><math id="footnote2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\text{poly}(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mtext>poly</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\text{poly}(N)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote2.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> decreases to zero with </span><math id="footnote2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote2.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">.
</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Our algorithm applies for the regime with large approximation factor, i.e., <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;\sqrt{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;\sqrt{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since we only want the nearest neighbors within distance <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cr</annotation></semantics></math> with the query point, we want to bound the probability of two points with distance greater than <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cr</annotation></semantics></math> to fall into the same bucket. Consider the family <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr_{g\in G}[g(x)=g(y)]\leq\frac{0.1}{N^{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>0.1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr_{g\in G}[g(x)=g(y)]\leq\frac{0.1}{N^{3}}</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x-y\|&gt;cr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x-y\|&gt;cr</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for each bucket, the expected number of collision (<math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y</annotation></semantics></math> fall into the same bucket and <math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x-y\|&gt;cr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x-y\|&gt;cr</annotation></semantics></math>) is less than <math id="A1.p2.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="N\cdot\Pr_{g\in G}[g(x)=g(y)]\leq\frac{0.1}{N^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>0.1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\cdot\Pr_{g\in G}[g(x)=g(y)]\leq\frac{0.1}{N^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, by Markov’s inequality, for each bucket, with probability greater than <math id="A1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{0.1}{N^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>0.1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{0.1}{N^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, there is no collision within the bucket. Then, by union bound over all the non-empty bucket (there are at most <math id="A1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> of them), with probablity greater than <math id="A1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{0.1}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>0.1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{0.1}{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, there is no collision in one hash table. By <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Indyk and Motwani (1998)</a></cite>, <math id="A1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=O(\log_{1/p_{2}}N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=O(\log_{1/p_{2}}N)</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., each hash function <math id="A1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in G</annotation></semantics></math> is composed of <math id="A1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log_{1/p_{2}}N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log_{1/p_{2}}N)</annotation></semantics></math> hash functions sampled from the LSH family <math id="A1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, which suffices to achieve <math id="A1.p2.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr_{g\in G}[g(x)=g(y)]\leq\frac{0.1}{N^{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>0.1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr_{g\in G}[g(x)=g(y)]\leq\frac{0.1}{N^{3}}</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="A1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x-y\|&gt;cr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x-y\|&gt;cr</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, since the probability of collision is very small, the success probability (when <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x-y\|\leq r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x-y\|\leq r</annotation></semantics></math>), namely <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p=\Pr_{g\in G}[g(x)=g(y)]=N^{-3\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\Pr_{g\in G}[g(x)=g(y)]=N^{-3\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> (recall that <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=\frac{\log 1/p_{1}}{\log 1/p_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=\frac{\log 1/p_{1}}{\log 1/p_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>), is also somewhat small.
However, we can boost the success probability by using multiple hash tables.
Let <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> denote the number of hash tables.
Then for each <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the probability of its <math id="A1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>-nearest neighbor <math id="A1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathcal{N}(q_{i},r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathcal{N}(q_{i},r)</annotation></semantics></math>) falls into different bucket with <math id="A1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> tables is upper bounded by <math id="A1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-p)^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-p)^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By union bound over all possible nearest neighbors and all <math id="A1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s, the failure probability is bounded by <math id="A1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{2}(1-p)^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{2}(1-p)^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume we want the failure probability to be less than some <math id="A1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then we want <math id="A1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{2}(1-p)^{\ell}\leq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{2}(1-p)^{\ell}\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Taking logarithm of both sides, and using a Taylor expansion of <math id="A1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1-x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1-x)</annotation></semantics></math> for sufficiently small <math id="A1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, we find that <math id="A1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=O(N^{3\rho}(\log N+\log 1/\delta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=O(N^{3\rho}(\log N+\log 1/\delta))</annotation></semantics></math> suffices for success probability <math id="A1.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, by union bound over all <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> hash tables, with probability <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{0.1}{N^{1-3\rho}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>0.1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{0.1}{N^{1-3\rho}}</annotation></semantics></math>, there is no collision in all the hash tables, which implies <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i,j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i,j}=0</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|k_{j}-q_{i}\|&gt;cr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|k_{j}-q_{i}\|&gt;cr</annotation></semantics></math>. By setting <math id="A1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\frac{0.1}{N^{1-3\rho}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>0.1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\frac{0.1}{N^{1-3\rho}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get <math id="A1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=O(N^{3\rho}\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=O(N^{3\rho}\log N)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the total failure probability <math id="A1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by <math id="A1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta+\frac{0.1}{N^{1-3\rho}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>0.1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta+\frac{0.1}{N^{1-3\rho}}</annotation></semantics></math> which is <math id="A1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/N^{1-3\rho})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/N^{1-3\rho})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|k_{j}-q_{i}\|\leq r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|k_{j}-q_{i}\|\leq r</annotation></semantics></math>, from the guarantee above, we know that <math id="A1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> collides with <math id="A1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> at least once in the <math id="A1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> hash bucket. This implies <math id="A1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i,j}\geq 1/\text{count}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mtext>count</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i,j}\geq 1/\text{count}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <span id="A1.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">count</span> is the number of all the collisions in the <math id="A1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> hash buckets that <math id="A1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> retrieves. In the worst case, all the <math id="A1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathcal{N}(q_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathcal{N}(q_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> collides with <math id="A1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in all <math id="A1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> hash tables except for <math id="A1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> only colliding once. Therefore, <math id="A1.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{count}\leq(\mathcal{N}(q_{i})-1)\cdot\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>count</mtext><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{count}\leq(\mathcal{N}(q_{i})-1)\cdot\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, and this gives us <math id="A1.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i,j}\geq\frac{1}{(\mathcal{N}(q_{i})-1)\cdot\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i,j}\geq\frac{1}{(\mathcal{N}(q_{i})-1)\cdot\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Runtime and memory usage.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">One can see that for each query, we need to evaluate <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N^{3\rho}\log_{1/p_{2}}N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N^{3\rho}\log_{1/p_{2}}N)</annotation></semantics></math> hash functions and compute sum of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional vectors, so the total runtime is <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(mN^{1+3\rho}\log_{1/p_{2}}N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(mN^{1+3\rho}\log_{1/p_{2}}N)</annotation></semantics></math>. During the preprocessing, we need to store <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{3\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{3\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> hash tables and the sum of values, each with at most <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> buckets, so the total memory is <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(mN^{1+3\rho}\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(mN^{1+3\rho}\log N)</annotation></semantics></math> bits. In fact, the space used can be further improved to <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(mN\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(mN\log N)</annotation></semantics></math> bits. Instead of maintaining <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> hash tables, one can just store 1 hash table of size <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(mN\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(mN\log N)</annotation></semantics></math> with each entry responsible for tracking the values for each query. For each round of hashing (<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> rounds in total), hash all queries using the hash functions and creates empty buckets for them. Then, hash each key, and if the key hashes to an existing query bucket, its value is added (along with a count). After processing keys, each query accumulates the values and counts from its corresponding bucket. We give the memory-efficient implementation in <a href="#alg2" title="In Runtime and memory usage. ‣ Appendix A Proof of ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Linear memory ANNA implementation with LSH family <math id="alg2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> hash tables, and <math id="alg2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> hash functions/table</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            Input <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            ANNA output for each of the query.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            Let <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=Q(X)_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=Q(X)_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{i}=K(X)_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{i}=K(X)_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="alg2.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}=V(X)_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}=V(X)_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="alg2.l3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
            Initialize an array of tuples <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A[i]\leftarrow(0,0),\forall i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A[i]\leftarrow(0,0),\forall i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg2.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
              Sample <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> hash functions <math id="alg2.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{u,1},h_{u,2},\dots,h_{u,z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{u,1},h_{u,2},\dots,h_{u,z}</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. from <math id="alg2.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
              Create empty hash table <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> indexed by hash codes of queries (below).

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each query <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
               Compute hash code <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{u}(q_{i})=(h_{u,1}(q_{i}),\dots,h_{u,z}(q_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{u}(q_{i})=(h_{u,1}(q_{i}),\dots,h_{u,z}(q_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
               Create an entry in <math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> indexed by <math id="alg2.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{u}(q_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{u}(q_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg2.l10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{u}[g_{u}(q_{i})]\leftarrow(0,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{u}[g_{u}(q_{i})]\leftarrow(0,0)</annotation></semantics></math>.
  
</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each key-value pair <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k_{j},v_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k_{j},v_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
               Compute hash code <math id="alg2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{u}(k_{j})=(h_{u,1}(k_{j}),h_{u,2}(k_{j}),\dots,h_{u,z}(k_{j}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{u}(k_{j})=(h_{u,1}(k_{j}),h_{u,2}(k_{j}),\dots,h_{u,z}(k_{j}))</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg2.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{u}[g_{u}(k_{j})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{u}[g_{u}(k_{j})]</annotation></semantics></math> exists in <math id="alg2.l13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="alg2.l13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> <math id="alg2.l13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{u}[g_{u}(k_{j})]\mathrel{+}=(v_{j},1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.056em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">+</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{u}[g_{u}(k_{j})]\mathrel{+}=(v_{j},1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
  
</div>
<div id="alg2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each query <math id="alg2.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg2.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A[i]\mathrel{+}=T_{u}[g_{u}(q_{i})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.056em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">+</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A[i]\mathrel{+}=T_{u}[g_{u}(q_{i})]</annotation></semantics></math>
  
</div>
<div id="alg2.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
              
              
            Initialize a dictionary <math id="alg2.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{attn}\leftarrow\{(q_{1},0),(q_{2},0),\ldots,(q_{N},0)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">attn</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{attn}\leftarrow\{(q_{1},0),(q_{2},0),\ldots,(q_{N},0)\}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each query <math id="alg2.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l17.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{attn}\leftarrow A[i][0]/A[i][1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">attn</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{attn}\leftarrow A[i][0]/A[i][1]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">19:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <span id="alg2.l19.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">attn</span>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>ANNA-transformer can simulate MPC</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our simulation of MPC using ANNA-transformers uses only a
special case of ANNA, which we call <em id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Exact Match Attention (<span id="A2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">EMA</span>)</em>.
In EMA, we require the key to be <em id="A2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exactly the same as</em> the query for it to be considered in the attention matrix.
We show that this special case already suffices to simulate MPC.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(EM Attention)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the input embedding, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K,V:\mathbb{R}^{N\times d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{N\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K,V:\mathbb{R}^{N\times d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{N\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be query/key/value embedding functions. For any query <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(q)=\{k_{j}\in K:k_{j}=q\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(q)=\{k_{j}\in K:k_{j}=q\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each query <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <em id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">Exact Match attention</em> computes</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{EMA}_{K,V}(q_{i})=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{|\mathcal{N}(q_{i})|}\displaystyle\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}(q_{i})}v_{j}&amp;\textup{if }\mathcal{N}(q_{i})\neq\emptyset\\
\hskip 50.00008pt\mathbf{0}&amp;\textup{otherwise.}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>EMA</mtext><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{EMA}_{K,V}(q_{i})=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{|\mathcal{N}(q_{i})|}\displaystyle\sum_{j\in\mathcal{N}(q_{i})}v_{j}&amp;\textup{if }\mathcal{N}(q_{i})\neq\emptyset\\
\hskip 50.00008pt\mathbf{0}&amp;\textup{otherwise.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">EMA layer and EMA-transformer are defined analogously. To see that EMA is a special case of ANNA, notice that in ANNA, we can set <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0,c\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0,c\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i,j}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{N}(q_{i})|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i,j}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{N}(q_{i})|}</annotation></semantics></math> such that it becomes exactly the same as EM attention. EMA also admits a near linear-time algorithm: sort all the keys first (using a lexicographic ordering) in time <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(dN\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(dN\log N)</annotation></semantics></math> and space <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(dN)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(dN)</annotation></semantics></math>; at query time, perform binary search in time <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(d\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(d\log N)</annotation></semantics></math> per query.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We first give a simulation that directly simulates the <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-round <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-MPC using <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=R+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=R+1</annotation></semantics></math> layers but large embedding dimensions to showcase the core idea of the proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(EMA simulates MPC)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For constant <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, any deterministic <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-round MPC protocol <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> machines with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=O(N^{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=O(N^{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> words local memory, there exists an EMA-transformer <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> with depth <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=R+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=R+1</annotation></semantics></math>, number of heads <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=O(N^{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=O(N^{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>, and embedding dimension <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(N^{5\varepsilon}\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(N^{5\varepsilon}\log N)</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(\mathtt{input})=\pi(\mathtt{input})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(\mathtt{input})=\pi(\mathtt{input})</annotation></semantics></math>
for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{input}\in\mathbb{Z}_{2^{p}}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℤ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msup><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{input}\in\mathbb{Z}_{2^{p}}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-round MPC protocol <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> machines that maps the <math id="A2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{input}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{input}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{output}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚘𝚞𝚝𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{output}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the intermediate steps for local computation phase and message transimission phase. We denote the input to all the machines before the local computation as <math id="A2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{MachineIn_{1}},\tt{MachineIn_{2}},\ldots,\tt{MachineIn_{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙸𝚗</mi><mn>𝟷</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙸𝚗</mi><mn>𝟸</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙸𝚗</mi><mi>𝚁</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{MachineIn_{1}},\tt{MachineIn_{2}},\ldots,\tt{MachineIn_{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and denote the information after deterministic local computations <math id="A2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tt{Local}_{r}^{i})_{r\in[R],i\in[N]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙻𝚘𝚌𝚊𝚕</mi><mi>𝚛</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚛</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝚁</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝚒</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝙽</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tt{Local}_{r}^{i})_{r\in[R],i\in[N]}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{MachineOut_{1}},\tt{MachineOut_{2}},\ldots,\tt{MachineOut_{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙾𝚞𝚝</mi><mn>𝟷</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙾𝚞𝚝</mi><mn>𝟸</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙾𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚁</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{MachineOut_{1}},\tt{MachineOut_{2}},\ldots,\tt{MachineOut_{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{MachineOut_{r}^{i}}=\tt{Local}_{r}^{i}(\tt{MachineIn_{r}^{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙾𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚛</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝙻𝚘𝚌𝚊𝚕</mi><mi>𝚛</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙸𝚗</mi><mi>𝚛</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{MachineOut_{r}^{i}}=\tt{Local}_{r}^{i}(\tt{MachineIn_{r}^{i}})</annotation></semantics></math>. In the communication (message transimission) phase, we need to route the messages to the correct machines ie from <math id="A2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{MachineOut_{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙾𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚛</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{MachineOut_{r}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{MachineIn_{r+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙸𝚗</mi><mrow><mi>𝚛</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>𝟷</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{MachineIn_{r+1}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">In our simulation, each token input to the EMA-transformer plays the role of a machine in the MPC protocol. We simulate the local computation functions <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tt{Local}_{r}^{i})_{r\in[R],i\in[N]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙻𝚘𝚌𝚊𝚕</mi><mi>𝚛</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚛</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝚁</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝚒</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝙽</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tt{Local}_{r}^{i})_{r\in[R],i\in[N]}</annotation></semantics></math> by the element-wise functions <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(\cdot),K(\cdot),V(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(\cdot),K(\cdot),V(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> in the architecture. Therefore, the simulation process can be partitioned into 3 different parts:</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Initialization. The <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{input}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{input}</annotation></semantics></math> feeded into EMA-transformer is distributed in the <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> tokens, and we need to transfer than into the first <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil{\frac{N}{s}}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil{\frac{N}{s}}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> tokens/machines to match <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{MachineIn_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙸𝚗</mi><mn>𝟷</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{MachineIn_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Routing (message transmission). After the local computation in each round <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, we need to communicate the messages from <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{MachineOut_{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙾𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚛</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{MachineOut_{r}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{MachineIn_{r+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙸𝚗</mi><mrow><mi>𝚛</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>𝟷</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{MachineIn_{r+1}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Final output. The MPC <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{output}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚘𝚞𝚝𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{output}</annotation></semantics></math> is distributed in the first <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil{\frac{N}{s}}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil{\frac{N}{s}}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> tokens/machines, and we need to distributed them back to the N tokens.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The following 3 lemmas construct the elements for each of these 3 parts.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first show the message transmission part of MPC can be simulate by the EMA-transformer. Recall that after <math id="A2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> rounds of local computation, each machine <math id="A2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> has a set of messages it wants to send to other machines, denoted by <math id="A2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{MachineOut}_{r}^{i}=\{(\tt{Msg}^{i}_{\tt{dest}},\tt{dest}):\tt{dest}\in\tt{sent}^{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙾𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚛</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐</mi><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝚜𝚎𝚗𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{MachineOut}_{r}^{i}=\{(\tt{Msg}^{i}_{\tt{dest}},\tt{dest}):\tt{dest}\in\tt{sent}^{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{sent}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝚜𝚎𝚗𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{sent}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of machine indices that machine <math id="A2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> will sent the message to and <math id="A2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{Msg}^{i}_{\tt{dest}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐</mi><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{Msg}^{i}_{\tt{dest}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the message machine <math id="A2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> send to machine <math id="A2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{dest}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{dest}</annotation></semantics></math>. After the message communication phase, each machine <math id="A2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> has the set of messages it receives from other machines, denoted by <math id="A2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{MachineIn}_{r+1}^{i}=\{(\tt{Msg},\tt{Src}):(\tt{Msg},i)\in\tt{MachineOut}_{r}^{\tt{Src}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙸𝚗</mi><mrow><mi>𝚛</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>𝟷</mn></mrow><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚂𝚛𝚌</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙾𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚛</mi><mi>𝚂𝚛𝚌</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{MachineIn}_{r+1}^{i}=\{(\tt{Msg},\tt{Src}):(\tt{Msg},i)\in\tt{MachineOut}_{r}^{\tt{Src}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since each machine can only send/receive <math id="A2.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> words, we have <math id="A2.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\tt{dest}\in\tt{sent}^{i}}|\tt{Msg}|\leq s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝚜𝚎𝚗𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝚜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\tt{dest}\in\tt{sent}^{i}}|\tt{Msg}|\leq s</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{(\tt{Msg},i)\in\tt{MachineOut}_{r}^{\tt{Src}}}|\tt{Msg}|\leq s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙾𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚛</mi><mi>𝚂𝚛𝚌</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝚜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{(\tt{Msg},i)\in\tt{MachineOut}_{r}^{\tt{Src}}}|\tt{Msg}|\leq s</annotation></semantics></math> for all machine <math id="A2.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. We call this process the routing process of MPC. The following lemma shows that each routing round of MPC can be simulated by one layer of EMA-transformer.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Routing)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any R-round MPC protocol <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> having <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> machines each with local memory <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in[R-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in[R-1]</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists an EMA-transformer <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{route}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚛𝚘𝚞𝚝𝚎</mi><mi>𝚛</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{route}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=O(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=O(s)</annotation></semantics></math> heads and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(\log q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(\log q)</annotation></semantics></math> for Q and K, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(s^{5}\log q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(s^{5}\log q)</annotation></semantics></math> for V that takes input <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\tt{MachineIn}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙸𝚗</mi><mi>𝚛</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\tt{MachineIn}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and produces output <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{route}_{r}(X)=\tt{MachineIn}_{r+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚛𝚘𝚞𝚝𝚎</mi><mi>𝚛</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚇</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙸𝚗</mi><mrow><mi>𝚛</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>𝟷</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{route}_{r}(X)=\tt{MachineIn}_{r+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Follow the assumption in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sanford et al. (2024c)</a></cite>, we encode the local computation into the element-wise operations <math id="A2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(\cdot),K(\cdot),V(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(\cdot),K(\cdot),V(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> of transformer. The main part of the proof will focus on using EMA to route <math id="A2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{MachineOut}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙾𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚛</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{MachineOut}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{MachineIn}_{r+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙸𝚗</mi><mrow><mi>𝚛</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>𝟷</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{MachineIn}_{r+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We assign a unique positional encoding or identifier to each machine <math id="A2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="A2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. This can be done with <math id="A2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log q)</annotation></semantics></math> bits. This encoding serves as a unique key to retrieve the message in each machine. The high level idea is to create a query for each machine <math id="A2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and a key for each <math id="A2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{dest}\in\tt{sent}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝚜𝚎𝚗𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{dest}\in\tt{sent}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and the associated value is the message <math id="A2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{Msg}^{i}_{dest}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐</mi><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{Msg}^{i}_{dest}</annotation></semantics></math> sent to <math id="A2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{dest}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{dest}</annotation></semantics></math> in the protocol. Since each machine can send at most <math id="A2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> messages to other machines, we create <math id="A2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> EMA heads and each head is responsible for one message for all the <math id="A2.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> machines. Each machine retrieves the message sent to them by having a query in each head. Because each query can attend only to perfectly matching keys, each distinct outbound message must be passed by a different attention head, but multiple inbound messages may be received by the same attention head.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Specifically, let <math id="A2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{h},K^{h},V^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{h},K^{h},V^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> be the query, key, value embedding after the machine local computation for each head <math id="A2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[s]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[s]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Set <math id="A2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{h}_{i}=p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{h}_{i}=p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, so</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{1}=Q^{2}=\cdots=Q^{s}=\begin{pmatrix}p_{1}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
p_{2}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
\vdots\\
p_{q}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>s</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{1}=Q^{2}=\cdots=Q^{s}=\begin{pmatrix}p_{1}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
p_{2}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
\vdots\\
p_{q}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{h}_{i}=p_{\tt{dest}^{i}_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚑</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{h}_{i}=p_{\tt{dest}^{i}_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{dest}^{i}_{h}\in\tt{sent}^{i}=\{\tt{dest}^{i}_{1},\tt{dest}^{i}_{2},\ldots,\tt{dest}^{i}_{s}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚑</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝚜𝚎𝚗𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mn>𝟷</mn><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mn>𝟸</mn><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚜</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{dest}^{i}_{h}\in\tt{sent}^{i}=\{\tt{dest}^{i}_{1},\tt{dest}^{i}_{2},\ldots,\tt{dest}^{i}_{s}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{dest}^{i}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚓</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{dest}^{i}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the destination machine index for the <math id="A2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>th word message that machine <math id="A2.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> sends. The key matrices are constructed as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="K^{1}=\begin{pmatrix}p_{\tt{dest}^{1}_{1}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
p_{\tt{dest}^{2}_{1}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
\vdots\\
p_{\tt{dest}^{q}_{1}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\end{pmatrix},\quad K^{2}=\begin{pmatrix}p_{\tt{dest}^{1}_{2}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
p_{\tt{dest}^{2}_{2}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
\cdots\\
p_{\tt{dest}^{q}_{2}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\end{pmatrix},\quad\ldots,\quad K^{s}=\begin{pmatrix}p_{\tt{dest}^{1}_{s}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
p_{\tt{dest}^{2}_{s}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
\vdots\\
p_{\tt{dest}^{q}_{s}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mn>𝟷</mn><mn>𝟷</mn></msubsup><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mn>𝟷</mn><mn>𝟸</mn></msubsup><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mn>𝟷</mn><mi>𝚚</mi></msubsup><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>K</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mn>𝟸</mn><mn>𝟷</mn></msubsup><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mn>𝟸</mn><mn>𝟸</mn></msubsup><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mn>𝟸</mn><mi>𝚚</mi></msubsup><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>K</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚜</mi><mn>𝟷</mn></msubsup><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚜</mi><mn>𝟸</mn></msubsup><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚜</mi><mi>𝚚</mi></msubsup><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{1}=\begin{pmatrix}p_{\tt{dest}^{1}_{1}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
p_{\tt{dest}^{2}_{1}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
\vdots\\
p_{\tt{dest}^{q}_{1}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\end{pmatrix},\quad K^{2}=\begin{pmatrix}p_{\tt{dest}^{1}_{2}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
p_{\tt{dest}^{2}_{2}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
\cdots\\
p_{\tt{dest}^{q}_{2}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\end{pmatrix},\quad\ldots,\quad K^{s}=\begin{pmatrix}p_{\tt{dest}^{1}_{s}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
p_{\tt{dest}^{2}_{s}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
\vdots\\
p_{\tt{dest}^{q}_{s}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{h}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{h}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be some embedding of <math id="A2.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tt{Msg}^{i}_{\tt{dest}^{i}_{h}},\tt{dest}^{i}_{h},i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚑</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚑</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tt{Msg}^{i}_{\tt{dest}^{i}_{h}},\tt{dest}^{i}_{h},i)</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="A2.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{h}_{i}=\tt{emb}_{i}^{h}(\tt{Msg}^{i}_{\tt{dest}^{i}_{h}},\tt{dest}^{i}_{h},i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚎𝚖𝚋</mi><mi>𝚒</mi><mi>𝚑</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚑</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚑</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{h}_{i}=\tt{emb}_{i}^{h}(\tt{Msg}^{i}_{\tt{dest}^{i}_{h}},\tt{dest}^{i}_{h},i)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A2.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{emb}_{i}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝚎𝚖𝚋</mi><mi>𝚒</mi><mi>𝚑</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{emb}_{i}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> defined later, and</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{1}=\begin{pmatrix}\tt{emb}_{1}^{1}(\tt{Msg}^{1}_{\tt{dest}^{1}_{1}},\tt{dest}^{1}_{1},1)\\
\tt{emb}_{2}^{1}(\tt{Msg}^{2}_{\tt{dest}^{2}_{1}},\tt{dest}^{2}_{1},2)\\
\vdots\\
\tt{emb}_{q}^{1}(\tt{Msg}^{q}_{\tt{dest}^{q}_{1}},\tt{dest}^{q}_{1},q)\end{pmatrix},\quad\ldots,\quad V^{s}=\begin{pmatrix}\tt{emb}_{1}^{s}(\tt{Msg}^{1}_{\tt{dest}^{1}_{s}},\tt{dest}^{1}_{s},1)\\
\tt{emb}_{2}^{s}(\tt{Msg}^{2}_{\tt{dest}^{2}_{s}},\tt{dest}^{2}_{s},2)\\
\vdots\\
\tt{emb}_{q}^{s}(\tt{Msg}^{q}_{\tt{dest}^{q}_{s}},\tt{dest}^{q}_{s},q)\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚎𝚖𝚋</mi><mn>𝟷</mn><mn>𝟷</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mn>𝟷</mn><mn>𝟷</mn></msubsup><mn>𝟷</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mn>𝟷</mn><mn>𝟷</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟷</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚎𝚖𝚋</mi><mn>𝟸</mn><mn>𝟷</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mn>𝟷</mn><mn>𝟸</mn></msubsup><mn>𝟸</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mn>𝟷</mn><mn>𝟸</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟸</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚎𝚖𝚋</mi><mi>𝚚</mi><mn>𝟷</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mn>𝟷</mn><mi>𝚚</mi></msubsup><mi>𝚚</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mn>𝟷</mn><mi>𝚚</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚎𝚖𝚋</mi><mn>𝟷</mn><mi>𝚜</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚜</mi><mn>𝟷</mn></msubsup><mn>𝟷</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚜</mi><mn>𝟷</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟷</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚎𝚖𝚋</mi><mn>𝟸</mn><mi>𝚜</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚜</mi><mn>𝟸</mn></msubsup><mn>𝟸</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚜</mi><mn>𝟸</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟸</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚎𝚖𝚋</mi><mi>𝚚</mi><mi>𝚜</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚜</mi><mi>𝚚</mi></msubsup><mi>𝚚</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚜</mi><mi>𝚚</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{1}=\begin{pmatrix}\tt{emb}_{1}^{1}(\tt{Msg}^{1}_{\tt{dest}^{1}_{1}},\tt{dest}^{1}_{1},1)\\
\tt{emb}_{2}^{1}(\tt{Msg}^{2}_{\tt{dest}^{2}_{1}},\tt{dest}^{2}_{1},2)\\
\vdots\\
\tt{emb}_{q}^{1}(\tt{Msg}^{q}_{\tt{dest}^{q}_{1}},\tt{dest}^{q}_{1},q)\end{pmatrix},\quad\ldots,\quad V^{s}=\begin{pmatrix}\tt{emb}_{1}^{s}(\tt{Msg}^{1}_{\tt{dest}^{1}_{s}},\tt{dest}^{1}_{s},1)\\
\tt{emb}_{2}^{s}(\tt{Msg}^{2}_{\tt{dest}^{2}_{s}},\tt{dest}^{2}_{s},2)\\
\vdots\\
\tt{emb}_{q}^{s}(\tt{Msg}^{q}_{\tt{dest}^{q}_{s}},\tt{dest}^{q}_{s},q)\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">By such construction of <math id="A2.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K,V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K,V</annotation></semantics></math>, in our EMA, each query will retrieve the average value of the messages whose key exactly matches the query.
However, by setting the value matrix this way, we might corrupt the message when there are more than one <math id="A2.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{h}_{i}\in K^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{h}_{i}\in K^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> that are equal to the same query.
To solve this problem, we can apply the same <em id="A2.p10.4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">multiple hashing-based encoding</em> in Lemma 3.2 from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sanford et al. (2024c)</a></cite>, which encodes each message in multiple fixed locations generated by a sparse binary matrix and have an extra “validity bit” indicating whether the message is corrupted or not. We restate an adapted version of their Lemma 3.2 here.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lemma 3.2 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sanford et al. (2024c)</a></cite>; message encoding in sparse averaging)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any message size <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, message count bound <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exist an encoding function <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> takes in <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tt{Msg}^{i}_{\tt{dest}^{i}_{h}},\tt{dest}^{i}_{h},i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚑</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚑</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tt{Msg}^{i}_{\tt{dest}^{i}_{h}},\tt{dest}^{i}_{h},i)</annotation></semantics></math> defined above where the size of it is bounded by <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[q]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[q]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[\alpha]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[\alpha]</annotation></semantics></math> and encodes it into <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{emb}_{i}^{h}(\tt{Msg}^{i}_{\tt{dest}^{i}_{h}},\tt{dest}^{i}_{h},i)\in\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚎𝚖𝚋</mi><mi>𝚒</mi><mi>𝚑</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚑</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚑</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>𝚖</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{emb}_{i}^{h}(\tt{Msg}^{i}_{\tt{dest}^{i}_{h}},\tt{dest}^{i}_{h},i)\in\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(\alpha^{4}\Delta\log q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(\alpha^{4}\Delta\log q)</annotation></semantics></math>, and a decoder function <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> takes in the output of the EMA with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K,V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K,V</annotation></semantics></math> defined above and decodes it into <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tt{Msg}^{i}_{\tt{dest}^{i}_{h}},\tt{dest}^{i}_{h},i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐</mi><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚑</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚑</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tt{Msg}^{i}_{\tt{dest}^{i}_{h}},\tt{dest}^{i}_{h},i)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{rcvd^{i}}=\{src_{1}^{i},src_{2}^{i},\ldots,src_{s}^{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝚛𝚌𝚟𝚍</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚜𝚛𝚌</mi><mn>𝟷</mn><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚜𝚛𝚌</mi><mn>𝟸</mn><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚜𝚛𝚌</mi><mi>𝚜</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{rcvd^{i}}=\{src_{1}^{i},src_{2}^{i},\ldots,src_{s}^{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{src}_{j}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝚜𝚛𝚌</mi><mi>𝚓</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{src}_{j}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>th source machine index that machine <math id="A2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> receives message from. Because <math id="A2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\tt{sent^{i}}|\leq s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝚜𝚎𝚗𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝚜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\tt{sent^{i}}|\leq s</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\tt{rcvd^{i}}|\leq s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝚛𝚌𝚟𝚍</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝚜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\tt{rcvd^{i}}|\leq s</annotation></semantics></math>, in each head of EMA, there are at most <math id="A2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> values get retrieved and averaged for each query. Thus, here we can just apply Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4 (Lemma 3.2 of ( ) ; message encoding in sparse averaging). ‣ Proof. ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B ANNA-transformer can simulate MPC ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a> with <math id="A2.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\Delta=s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\Delta=s</annotation></semantics></math>, which gives us an embedding dimension bound <math id="A2.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(s^{5}\log q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(s^{5}\log q)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">We then show with one layer EMA-transformer, we can properly initialize the setup of MPC by converting Input <math id="A2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=(\tt{input}_{1},input_{2},\ldots,input_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mn>𝟷</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mn>𝟸</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚗</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=(\tt{input}_{1},input_{2},\ldots,input_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{MachineIn}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙸𝚗</mi><mn>𝟷</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{MachineIn}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the input before the first round of MPC computation, ie the input is distributed evenly on the first <math id="A2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil{\frac{n}{s}}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil{\frac{n}{s}}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> machines.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.5</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Initialization)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-round MPC protocol <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> having <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> machines each with local memory <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-word input, there exists an EMA-transformer <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{init}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚒𝚝</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{init}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=1</annotation></semantics></math> head, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(\log q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(\log q)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(s)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> that takes <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{input}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{input}</annotation></semantics></math> and outputs <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{init}(input)=MachineIn_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚒𝚝</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙸𝚗</mi><mi>𝚛</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{init}(input)=MachineIn_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">The input should be distributed accross each machine <math id="A2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq\lceil{\frac{n}{s}}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq\lceil{\frac{n}{s}}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.p13.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tt{MachineIn}^{i}_{1}=\{(input_{idx},idx):idx\in s(i-1)+1,\ldots,\min\{n,si\}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙸𝚗</mi><mn>𝟷</mn><mi>𝚒</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝚜</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚒</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>𝟷</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>𝟷</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝚗</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚜𝚒</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{MachineIn}^{i}_{1}=\{(input_{idx},idx):idx\in s(i-1)+1,\ldots,\min\{n,si\}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{in}=\lceil{\frac{n}{s}}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{in}=\lceil{\frac{n}{s}}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of machines to store the initial input. Since the input given to <math id="A2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{init}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚒𝚝</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{init}</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="A2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> tokens (here we treat each token as a machine), we need to rearange the memory so that the input is distributed on the first <math id="A2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{in}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{in}</annotation></semantics></math> tokens.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Same as before, we use the positional encoding <math id="A2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the unique identifier for each machine. We create a key value pair for each input token and the key corresponds to the identifier of the machine that <math id="A2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{input}_{idx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{input}_{idx}</annotation></semantics></math> goes to and the value be <math id="A2.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tt{input}_{idx},idx)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tt{input}_{idx},idx)</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, create a query for each machine <math id="A2.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[q_{in}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[q_{in}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">For each machine <math id="A2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[q_{in}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[q_{in}]</annotation></semantics></math>, define the query embedding <math id="A2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\begin{pmatrix}p_{1}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
p_{2}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
\vdots\\
p_{q_{in}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\end{pmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\begin{pmatrix}p_{1}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
p_{2}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
\vdots\\
p_{q_{in}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">For each token <math id="A2.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{input}_{idx},idx\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝚗</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{input}_{idx},idx\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A2.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{dest}_{idx}=\lceil{\frac{idx}{s}}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi><mi>𝚜</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{dest}_{idx}=\lceil{\frac{idx}{s}}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> be the machine storing the token, define the key embedding <math id="A2.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\tt{idx}}=p_{\tt{dest}_{idx}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\tt{idx}}=p_{\tt{dest}_{idx}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\begin{pmatrix}p_{\tt{dest}_{1}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
p_{\tt{dest}_{2}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
\vdots\\
p_{\tt{dest}_{n}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\end{pmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mn>𝟷</mn></msub><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mn>𝟸</mn></msub><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚝</mi><mi>𝚗</mi></msub><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\begin{pmatrix}p_{\tt{dest}_{1}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
p_{\tt{dest}_{2}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
\vdots\\
p_{\tt{dest}_{n}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p15.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p15.3.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{\prime}=\tt{idx}\mod s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi><mo>mod</mo><mi>𝚜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{\prime}=\tt{idx}\mod s</annotation></semantics></math>. For each token <math id="A2.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{input}_{idx},idx\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝚗</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{input}_{idx},idx\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, define the value embedding <math id="A2.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\tt{idx}}\in\mathbb{R}^{2s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\tt{idx}}\in\mathbb{R}^{2s}</annotation></semantics></math> to be <math id="A2.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tt{input}_{idx},idx)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tt{input}_{idx},idx)</annotation></semantics></math> in the <math id="A2.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2i^{\prime}-1,2i^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2i^{\prime}-1,2i^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>-th entry and 0 in all other entry,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\begin{pmatrix}\tt{input}_{1}&amp;1&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;\tt{input}_{2}&amp;2&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;\tt{input}_{s}&amp;s\\
\tt{input}_{s+1}&amp;s+1&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\end{pmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mn>𝟷</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mn>𝟸</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚜</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mi>s</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mrow><mi>𝚜</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>𝟷</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\begin{pmatrix}\tt{input}_{1}&amp;1&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;\tt{input}_{2}&amp;2&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;\tt{input}_{s}&amp;s\\
\tt{input}_{s+1}&amp;s+1&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\ldots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p15.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p15.4.1" class="ltx_text">By setting the value matrix like this, we can avoid corrupting the messages.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Last, we show that with an additional one layer EMA-transformer, we can map the final round <math id="A2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{MachineIn}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙸𝚗</mi><mi>𝚁</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{MachineIn}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> to the <math id="A2.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{output}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚘𝚞𝚝𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{output}</annotation></semantics></math> of MPC protocol where the output is store in the first <math id="A2.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil{\frac{n}{s}}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil{\frac{n}{s}}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> machines.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.6</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Final Output)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any R-round MPC protocol <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> having <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> machines each with local memory <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-word input, there exists an EMA-transformer <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{out}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚘𝚞𝚝</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{out}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=1</annotation></semantics></math> head, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(\log q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(\log q)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(s)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> that takes <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{MachineIn}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙸𝚗</mi><mi>𝚁</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{MachineIn}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and outputs <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tt{out}(\tt{MachineIn}_{R})_{:n}=\pi(\tt{input})=\tt{output}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚘𝚞𝚝</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙸𝚗</mi><mi>𝚁</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>𝚗</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝚘𝚞𝚝𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{out}(\tt{MachineIn}_{R})_{:n}=\pi(\tt{input})=\tt{output}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, the element-wise operations can compute <math id="A2.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{MachineOut}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙾𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚁</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{MachineOut}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{MachineIn}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙸𝚗</mi><mi>𝚁</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{MachineIn}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. The output is distributed accross each machine <math id="A2.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq\lceil{\frac{n}{s}}\rceil=q_{out}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq\lceil{\frac{n}{s}}\rceil=q_{out}</annotation></semantics></math> with memory of machine <math id="A2.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="A2.p17.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tt{output}^{i}=\{(\tt{output}_{idx},idx):idx\in s(i-1)+1,\ldots,\min\{n,si\}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝚘𝚞𝚝𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚘𝚞𝚝𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝚜</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚒</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>𝟷</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>𝟷</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝚗</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚜𝚒</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{output}^{i}=\{(\tt{output}_{idx},idx):idx\in s(i-1)+1,\ldots,\min\{n,si\}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we just need to retrieve the output tokens from all the <math id="A2.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{out}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{out}</annotation></semantics></math> machines and distribute them back to <math id="A2.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> tokens. This step does the inverse job of init. We create a query for each token <math id="A2.p17.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{output}_{idx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚘𝚞𝚝𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{output}_{idx}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.p17.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{idx}\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝚗</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{idx}\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.p17.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{src}_{idx}=\lceil{\frac{idx}{s}}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚜𝚛𝚌</mi><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi><mi>𝚜</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{src}_{idx}=\lceil{\frac{idx}{s}}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> be the machine token <math id="A2.p17.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{output}_{idx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚘𝚞𝚝𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{output}_{idx}</annotation></semantics></math> is in.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">For each token <math id="A2.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{output}_{idx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚘𝚞𝚝𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{output}_{idx}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{idx}\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝚗</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{idx}\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, define the query embedding <math id="A2.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\tt{idx}}=p_{\tt{src}_{idx}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>𝚜𝚛𝚌</mi><mi>𝚒𝚍𝚡</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\tt{idx}}=p_{\tt{src}_{idx}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\begin{pmatrix}p_{\tt{src}_{1}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
p_{\tt{src}_{2}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
\vdots\\
p_{\tt{src}_{n}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\end{pmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>𝚜𝚛𝚌</mi><mn>𝟷</mn></msub><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>𝚜𝚛𝚌</mi><mn>𝟸</mn></msub><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>𝚜𝚛𝚌</mi><mi>𝚗</mi></msub><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\begin{pmatrix}p_{\tt{src}_{1}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
p_{\tt{src}_{2}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
\vdots\\
p_{\tt{src}_{n}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p18.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p18.2.1" class="ltx_text">For each machine <math id="A2.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[q_{out}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[q_{out}]</annotation></semantics></math>, create a key <math id="A2.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{i}=p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{i}=p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\begin{pmatrix}p_{1}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
p_{2}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
\vdots\\
p_{q_{out}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\end{pmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\begin{pmatrix}p_{1}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
p_{2}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\\
\vdots\\
p_{q_{out}}^{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p18.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p18.3.1" class="ltx_text">The value associates with each key <math id="A2.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is the memory <math id="A2.p18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{MsgOut}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐𝙾𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{MsgOut}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> stored in each machine <math id="A2.p18.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the value embedding <math id="A2.p18.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}=\tt{MsgOut}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐𝙾𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}=\tt{MsgOut}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\begin{pmatrix}\tt{MsgOut}_{1}\\
\tt{MsgOut}_{2}\\
\vdots\\
\tt{MsgOut}_{q_{out}}\end{pmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐𝙾𝚞𝚝</mi><mn>𝟷</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐𝙾𝚞𝚝</mi><mn>𝟸</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝙼𝚜𝚐𝙾𝚞𝚝</mi><msub><mi>𝚚</mi><mi>𝚘𝚞𝚝</mi></msub></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\begin{pmatrix}\tt{MsgOut}_{1}\\
\tt{MsgOut}_{2}\\
\vdots\\
\tt{MsgOut}_{q_{out}}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p18.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p18.4.1" class="ltx_text">By choosing a proper element-wise function <math id="A2.p18.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>, out(<math id="A2.p18.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{MachineIn}_{R})_{i,1}=output_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><msub><mi>𝙼𝚊𝚌𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚎𝙸𝚗</mi><mi>𝚁</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝚒</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟷</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝚘𝚞𝚝𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{MachineIn}_{R})_{i,1}=output_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">The theorem follows from stacking the elements from these three lemmas.
Each lemma gives us a single layer of the final EMA-transformer <math id="A2.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> with embedding dimension <math id="A2.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(N^{5\varepsilon}\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(N^{5\varepsilon}\log N)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T=\tt{out}\circ route_{R-1}\circ\cdots\circ route_{1}\circ init\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝚘𝚞𝚝</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>𝚛𝚘𝚞𝚝𝚎</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝚁</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>𝟷</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>𝚛𝚘𝚞𝚝𝚎</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>𝟷</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚒𝚝</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" lspace="0em" mathvariant="monospace" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\tt{out}\circ route_{R-1}\circ\cdots\circ route_{1}\circ init\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark B.7</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(General <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-MPC)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The above simulation works the same for <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-MPC by padding <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max(0,O(N^{1+\gamma-\varepsilon})-N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max(0,O(N^{1+\gamma-\varepsilon})-N)</annotation></semantics></math> empty chain-of-thought tokens in the input.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark B.8</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Number of heads)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The standard transformer can simulate MPC using the same embedding dimension but only <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> attention head <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sanford et al. (2024c)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sanford et al. (2024a)</a></cite>. Here the EMA needs <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N^{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N^{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> heads, and we leave how to improve the number of heads for future work.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p20.1" class="ltx_p">Since EM attention is a special case of ANN attention with <math id="A2.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, the simulation of MPC with ANNA-transformer naturally follows from Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem B.2 (EMA simulates MPC). ‣ Appendix B ANNA-transformer can simulate MPC ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary B.9</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(ANNA simulates MPC)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For constant <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, any deterministic <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-round MPC protocol <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> machines with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=O(N^{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=O(N^{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> words local memory, there exists an ANNA-transformer <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> with depth <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=R+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=R+1</annotation></semantics></math>, number of heads <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=O(N^{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=O(N^{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>, and embedding dimension <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(N^{5\varepsilon}\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(N^{5\varepsilon}\log N)</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(\mathtt{input})=\pi(\mathtt{input})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(\mathtt{input})=\pi(\mathtt{input})</annotation></semantics></math>
for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{input}\in\mathbb{Z}_{2^{p}}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℤ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msup><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{input}\in\mathbb{Z}_{2^{p}}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p21.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem B.2 (EMA simulates MPC). ‣ Appendix B ANNA-transformer can simulate MPC ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> only gives us an MPC simulation in the sublinear local memory regime when <math id="A2.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=O(N^{1/5-\delta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=O(N^{1/5-\delta})</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. However, a lot of MPC protocol algorithms require <math id="A2.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=\Omega(N^{1/2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=\Omega(N^{1/2})</annotation></semantics></math> local, such as MPC algorithm for 3-SUM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hajiaghayi et al. (2019)</a></cite> and algorithms for graphs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sanford et al. (2024a)</a></cite>. The above simulation using EMA-transformer does not yield a sublinear embedding dimension. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sanford et al. (2024a)</a></cite> further gives a simulation of MPC with sublinear local memory using transformer with sublinear embedding dimension by simulating one round of MPC protocol with <math id="A2.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> layers of transformer, instead of just one layer. Their improvement also applies here.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.10</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(EMA simulates MPC with improved embedding dimension)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For constant <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, any deterministic <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-round MPC protocol <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> machines with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=O(N^{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=O(N^{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> words local memory, there exists an EMA-transformer of depth <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=O(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=O(R)</annotation></semantics></math>, number of heads <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=O(N^{\frac{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon}{4}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=O(N^{\frac{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon}{4}})</annotation></semantics></math> and embedding dimension <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(\mathtt{input})=\pi(\mathtt{input})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(\mathtt{input})=\pi(\mathtt{input})</annotation></semantics></math>
for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{input}\in\mathbb{Z}_{2^{p}}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℤ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msup><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{input}\in\mathbb{Z}_{2^{p}}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof relies on simulating any MPC protocol by a restricted version of MPC protocol <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sanford et al. (2024a)</a></cite> which limits the number of machines each machine can send message to. Then, use a modified version of Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem B.2 (EMA simulates MPC). ‣ Appendix B ANNA-transformer can simulate MPC ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> to simulate this restricted version of MPC.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.11</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Definition 3 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sanford et al. (2024a)</a></cite>)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For constants <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma,\varepsilon,\rho&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma,\varepsilon,\rho&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, a <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,\varepsilon,\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,\varepsilon,\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>-MPC protocol is a <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-MPC protocol with an additional constraint: in each round, each machine can only send/receive messages from <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=O(n^{\rho})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=O(n^{\rho})</annotation></semantics></math> machines, while the total size of messages it can send and receive is still <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=O(N^{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=O(N^{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>. We refer to <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> as the <em id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">communication capacity</em>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sanford et al. (2024a)</a></cite><span id="A2.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text"> gives a construction that simulates a R-round <math id="A2.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-MPC protocol with <math id="A2.p23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(R)</annotation></semantics></math>-round <math id="A2.p23.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,\varepsilon,\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,\varepsilon,\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>-MPC protocol. We restate their proposition here.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.12</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Proposition 24 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sanford et al. (2024a)</a></cite>; <math id="A2.Thmtheorem12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,\varepsilon,\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,\varepsilon,\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>-MPC simulates <math id="A2.Thmtheorem12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-MPC)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For constants <math id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma,\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma,\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in(0,\varepsilon/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in(0,\varepsilon/2)</annotation></semantics></math>, if function <math id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> can be computed by an R-round <math id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-MPC, it can also be computed by a <math id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{R(1+\gamma)^{2}}{\rho^{2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{R(1+\gamma)^{2}}{\rho^{2}})</annotation></semantics></math>-round <math id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,\varepsilon,\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,\varepsilon,\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>-MPC protocol.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we just need to simulate <math id="A2.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,\varepsilon,\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,\varepsilon,\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>-MPC protocol using our EMA-transformer. The simulation follows the same recipe as Thereom <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem B.2 (EMA simulates MPC). ‣ Appendix B ANNA-transformer can simulate MPC ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, where we have the initialization, message passing and final output phase. Since the initialization and output of <math id="A2.p24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,\varepsilon,\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,\varepsilon,\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>-MPC follow the same rule as <math id="A2.p24.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-MPC, we only need to modify the message passing part of the simulation which corresponds to the routing Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3 (Routing). ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B ANNA-transformer can simulate MPC ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.13</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(EMA simulates <math id="A2.Thmtheorem13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,\varepsilon,\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,\varepsilon,\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>-MPC)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For constant <math id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\rho&lt;\varepsilon&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\rho&lt;\varepsilon&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, any deterministic <math id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-round MPC protocol <math id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> machines with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=O(N^{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=O(N^{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> words local memory and communication capacity <math id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=O(N^{\rho})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=O(N^{\rho})</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists an EMA-transformer of depth <math id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=R+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=R+1</annotation></semantics></math>, number of heads <math id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=O(N^{\rho})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=O(N^{\rho})</annotation></semantics></math> and embedding dimension <math id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(N^{\varepsilon+4\rho}\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(N^{\varepsilon+4\rho}\log N)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(\mathtt{input})=\pi(\mathtt{input})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(\mathtt{input})=\pi(\mathtt{input})</annotation></semantics></math>
for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{input}\in\mathbb{Z}_{2^{p}}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℤ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msup><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{input}\in\mathbb{Z}_{2^{p}}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.3.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the initialization and final output part, we just use the same <math id="A2.p25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{init}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚒𝚝</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{init}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{out}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚘𝚞𝚝</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{out}</annotation></semantics></math> constructed in Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma B.5 (Initialization). ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B ANNA-transformer can simulate MPC ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma B.6 (Final Output). ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B ANNA-transformer can simulate MPC ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>. In the routing part (Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3 (Routing). ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B ANNA-transformer can simulate MPC ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>), because <math id="A2.p25.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\tt{sent}^{i}|\leq k,|\tt{rcvd}^{i}|\leq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝚜𝚎𝚗𝚝</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝚔</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝚛𝚌𝚟𝚍</mi><mi>𝚒</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝚔</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\tt{sent}^{i}|\leq k,|\tt{rcvd}^{i}|\leq k</annotation></semantics></math>, we only need <math id="A2.p25.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> heads and in each head of EMA, there are at most <math id="A2.p25.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> keys matching each query and thus at most <math id="A2.p25.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> values get averaged for a single query. Therefore, we can apply Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4 (Lemma 3.2 of ( ) ; message encoding in sparse averaging). ‣ Proof. ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B ANNA-transformer can simulate MPC ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a> with <math id="A2.p25.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p25.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=s</annotation></semantics></math>, leading to an embedding dimension <math id="A2.p25.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(N^{\varepsilon+4\rho}\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(N^{\varepsilon+4\rho}\log N)</annotation></semantics></math>. This gives us a new <math id="A2.p25.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tt{route}^{\prime}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝚛𝚘𝚞𝚝𝚎</mi><mi>𝚛</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tt{route}^{\prime}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> with reduced number of heads and embedding dimension for each round <math id="A2.p25.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p26.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p26.1.1" class="ltx_text">Likewise, we stack the 3 building blocks of one-layer EMA-transformer and have an <math id="A2.p26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(R+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(R+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-layer EMA transformer</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T=\tt{out}\circ route^{\prime}_{R-1}\circ\cdots\circ route^{\prime}_{1}\circ init" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝚘𝚞𝚝</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>𝚛𝚘𝚞𝚝𝚎</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝚁</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>𝟷</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>𝚛𝚘𝚞𝚝𝚎</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>𝟷</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚒𝚝</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\tt{out}\circ route^{\prime}_{R-1}\circ\cdots\circ route^{\prime}_{1}\circ init</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p26.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p26.2.1" class="ltx_text">and this finishes the construction for the lemma.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p27" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.p27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=\min(\varepsilon/2,(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)/4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=\min(\varepsilon/2,(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)/4)</annotation></semantics></math>. In this setting, <math id="A2.p27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem12" title="Lemma B.12 (Proposition 24 of ( ) ; (𝛾,𝜀,𝜌)-MPC simulates (𝛾,𝜀)-MPC). ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B ANNA-transformer can simulate MPC ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.12</span></a>, we can simulate the <math id="A2.p27.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-round <math id="A2.p27.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-MPC by an <math id="A2.p27.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}=O(\frac{R(1+\varepsilon)^{2}}{\min(\varepsilon^{2},(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)^{2})})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}=O(\frac{R(1+\varepsilon)^{2}}{\min(\varepsilon^{2},(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)^{2})})</annotation></semantics></math>-round <math id="A2.p27.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,\varepsilon,\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,\varepsilon,\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>-MPC. Then, by Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem13" title="Lemma B.13 (EMA simulates (𝛾,𝜀,𝜌)-MPC). ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B ANNA-transformer can simulate MPC ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.13</span></a>, we can simulate this <math id="A2.p27.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>-round <math id="A2.p27.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,\varepsilon,\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,\varepsilon,\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>-MPC by an <math id="A2.p27.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}+1</annotation></semantics></math>-layer EMA transformer with <math id="A2.p27.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N^{\rho})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N^{\rho})</annotation></semantics></math> heads and embedding dimension <math id="A2.p27.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N^{\varepsilon+4\rho}\log N)=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N^{\varepsilon+4\rho}\log N)=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p28" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p28.1" class="ltx_p">Again, the improved simulation result of ANNA-transformer follows from Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem10" title="Theorem B.10 (EMA simulates MPC with improved embedding dimension). ‣ Appendix B ANNA-transformer can simulate MPC ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.10</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary B.14</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(ANNA simulates MPC with improved embedding dimension)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For constant <math id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, any deterministic <math id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-round MPC protocol <math id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> machines with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=O(N^{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=O(N^{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> words local memory, there exists an ANNA-transformer of depth <math id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=O(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=O(R)</annotation></semantics></math>, number of heads <math id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=O(N^{\frac{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon}{4}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=O(N^{\frac{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon}{4}})</annotation></semantics></math> and embedding dimension <math id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(\mathtt{input})=\pi(\mathtt{input})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(\mathtt{input})=\pi(\mathtt{input})</annotation></semantics></math>
for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{input}\in\mathbb{Z}_{2^{p}}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℤ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msup><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{input}\in\mathbb{Z}_{2^{p}}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>MPC can Simulate ANNA-transformer</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As a warm-up, we first simulate EMA-transformers using MPC, and then generalize it to the simulation of ANNA-transformers.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(MPC simulates EMA)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix constants <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-layer EMA-transformer <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="mH=O(N^{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">mH=O(N^{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{L}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{L}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>-round MPC protocol <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> with local memory <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=O(N^{1+\varepsilon-\varepsilon^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=O(N^{1+\varepsilon-\varepsilon^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> machines such that
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(\mathtt{input})=T(\mathtt{input})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\mathtt{input})=T(\mathtt{input})</annotation></semantics></math> for all
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{input}\in\mathbb{Z}_{2^{p}}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℤ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msup><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{input}\in\mathbb{Z}_{2^{p}}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first show how to use MPC to simulate one layer of EMA-transformer. In the high level, for each token <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have a token Machine <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> which is responsible for computing the key, query and value embedding for <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and other element-wise computation on <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. The main bulk of the proof is to search for the exact matching keys for each query and send the averaged values associated with the matching keys to the token machines. In order to do this, we sort all the key and value pairs <math id="A3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k_{i},v_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k_{i},v_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> in the order defined by the key. We divide the sorted key and value pairs into buckets such that each bucket contains the same keys. For each bucket, we have a “meta-info" machine to store the indices of the machines that contains the keys in the bucket. We then compute the averaged values within each bucket and store the averaged value into the “meta-info" machine and propagate the value to all the queries that match with the key.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">To begin with, let <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the space of query and key, and we define a comparator <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> in order to sort. Without loss of generality, we just define it to be the lexicographical ordering comparator. Based on this comparator, we define a query ranking permutation of <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[N]</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=(\sigma_{1},\sigma_{2},\ldots,\sigma_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=(\sigma_{1},\sigma_{2},\ldots,\sigma_{N})</annotation></semantics></math> and a key ranking permutation of <math id="A3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[N]</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{\prime}=(\sigma_{1}^{\prime},\sigma_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,\sigma_{N}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{\prime}=(\sigma_{1}^{\prime},\sigma_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,\sigma_{N}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q_{\sigma_{1}}&lt;q_{\sigma_{2}}&lt;\cdots&lt;q_{\sigma_{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{\sigma_{1}}&lt;q_{\sigma_{2}}&lt;\cdots&lt;q_{\sigma_{N}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex19.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">and</span> </td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle k_{\sigma_{1}^{\prime}}&lt;k_{\sigma_{2}^{\prime}}&lt;\cdots&lt;k_{\sigma_{N}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle k_{\sigma_{1}^{\prime}}&lt;k_{\sigma_{2}^{\prime}}&lt;\cdots&lt;k_{\sigma_{N}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the“meta-info" machine, we use a uniform hash function <math id="A3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:\mathcal{X}\rightarrow[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:\mathcal{X}\rightarrow[N]</annotation></semantics></math> to map queries and keys to their corresponding “meta-info" machine. Recall that for a uniform hash function <math id="A3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(h(a)=h(b))=\frac{1}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(h(a)=h(b))=\frac{1}{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="A3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\neq b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\neq b</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\exists i\;\text{such that the size of bucket }h(q_{i})\geq s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>such that the size of bucket </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\exists i\;\text{such that the size of bucket }h(q_{i})\geq s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{P}(\exists s\;\text{different elements fall into one bucket})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>different elements fall into one bucket</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{P}(\exists s\;\text{different elements fall into one bucket})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\binom{N}{s}\frac{1}{N^{s}}\leq\frac{1}{s!}=\frac{1}{N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}}!}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\binom{N}{s}\frac{1}{N^{s}}\leq\frac{1}{s!}=\frac{1}{N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}}!}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">With high probability, each “meta-info" machine is responsible for at most <math id="A3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> keys or queries.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We divide the machines into different types and summarize the role of each type of machine here:</span></p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, Machine <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is the <span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">token machine</span> for <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. This machine performs all the element-wise computation for token <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, it computes the query, key, value embeddings <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i},k_{i},v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i},k_{i},v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and element-wise operations after the attention layer.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[\lceil{mN/s}\rceil]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[\lceil{mN/s}\rceil]</annotation></semantics></math>, Machine <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,Q)</annotation></semantics></math> is a data structure machine for sorting queries and storing the <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>th chunk of the sorted list of queries after sorting. In other words, let <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{q}=\lfloor{s/m}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{q}=\lfloor{s/m}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of queries each machine can store and, at the end of sorting, machine <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,Q)</annotation></semantics></math> stores <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{q_{\sigma_{(i-1)\cdot n_{q}+1}},\ldots,q_{\sigma_{i\cdot n_{q}}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{q_{\sigma_{(i-1)\cdot n_{q}+1}},\ldots,q_{\sigma_{i\cdot n_{q}}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\lceil{2mN/s}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\lceil{2mN/s}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>, Machine <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,KV)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,KV)</annotation></semantics></math> is a data structure machine for sorted list of key and value pairs. In other words, let <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{k}=\lfloor{s/2m}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{k}=\lfloor{s/2m}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of key and value pairs each machine can store and, at the end of sorting, machine <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,KV)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,KV)</annotation></semantics></math> stores <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(k_{\sigma^{\prime}_{(i-1)\cdot n_{q}+1}},v_{\sigma^{\prime}_{(i-1)\cdot n_{q}+1}}),\ldots,(k_{\sigma^{\prime}_{i\cdot n_{q}}},v_{\sigma^{\prime}_{i\cdot n_{q}}})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(k_{\sigma^{\prime}_{(i-1)\cdot n_{q}+1}},v_{\sigma^{\prime}_{(i-1)\cdot n_{q}+1}}),\ldots,(k_{\sigma^{\prime}_{i\cdot n_{q}}},v_{\sigma^{\prime}_{i\cdot n_{q}}})\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, Machine <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,h_{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,h_{q})</annotation></semantics></math> is the “meta-info" machine for the queries whose hash value is <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h_{q}^{i}=\{q_{j}|j\in[N],h(q_{j})=i\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{q}^{i}=\{q_{j}|j\in[N],h(q_{j})=i\}</annotation></semantics></math>. This machine stores the location information of <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in h_{q}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in h_{q}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in the sorted list. Specifically, for all <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in h_{q}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in h_{q}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, this machine stores the start machine index, i.e. (start, Q) where <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textup{start}=\argmin_{j}\{q\in" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>start</mtext><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{start}=\argmin_{j}\{q\in</annotation></semantics></math> Machine <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j,Q)</annotation></semantics></math>}, and the end machine index, i.e. (end, Q) where <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textup{end}=\arg\max_{j}\{q\in" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>end</mtext><mo>=</mo><mi>arg</mi><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{end}=\arg\max_{j}\{q\in</annotation></semantics></math> Machine <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j,Q)</annotation></semantics></math>}.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, Machine <math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,h_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,h_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> is the “meta-info" machine for the keys whose hash value is <math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h_{k}^{i}=\{k_{j}|j\in[N],h(k_{j})=i\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k}^{i}=\{k_{j}|j\in[N],h(k_{j})=i\}</annotation></semantics></math>. This machine stores the location information of <math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in h_{k}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in h_{k}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in the sorted list. Specifically, for all <math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in h_{q}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in h_{q}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, this machine stores the start machine index, i.e. (start, KV) where <math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textup{start}=\argmin_{j}\{k\in" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>start</mtext><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{start}=\argmin_{j}\{k\in</annotation></semantics></math> Machine <math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j,KV)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j,KV)</annotation></semantics></math>}, and the end machine index, i.e. (end, Q) where <math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textup{end}=\arg\max_{j}\{k\in" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>end</mtext><mo>=</mo><mi>arg</mi><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{end}=\arg\max_{j}\{k\in</annotation></semantics></math> Machine <math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j,KV)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j,KV)</annotation></semantics></math>}.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The auxiliary machines needed for message propagation.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We proceed to discuss the MPC protocol for computing the output of one layer single head EM-attention transformer. In the first round, (same as the token dispersion stage of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sanford et al. (2024c)</a></cite>), route each token <math id="A3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to its corresponding token machine <math id="A3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">In the second round, each token machine <math id="A3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> computes the query, key value embedding <math id="A3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=Q(x_{i}),k_{i}=K(x_{i}),v_{i}=V(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=Q(x_{i}),k_{i}=K(x_{i}),v_{i}=V(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and sends <math id="A3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{i},i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{i},i)</annotation></semantics></math> to the sorting query data structure machine <math id="A3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lceil{mi/s}\rceil,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lceil{mi/s}\rceil,Q)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k_{i},v_{i},i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k_{i},v_{i},i)</annotation></semantics></math> to the sorting key data structure machine <math id="A3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lceil{2mi/s}\rceil,KV)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lceil{2mi/s}\rceil,KV)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, sorting query data structure machines (<math id="A3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,Q)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\lceil{mN/s}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\lceil{mN/s}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>) sorts the queries. Sorting in MPC has been well studied, and this can be done in constant number of rounds <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Goodrich et al. (2011)</a></cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(MPC Sorting)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists an MPC protocol with local memory <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> that can sort <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> items and each item has size <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N^{\varepsilon}),\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N^{\varepsilon}),\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> rounds with <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N^{1+\varepsilon-\varepsilon^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N^{1+\varepsilon-\varepsilon^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> machines.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">After sorting, for each <math id="A3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, we need to send the location information of <math id="A3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, ie which data structure machines contains <math id="A3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, to its “meta-info” machine <math id="A3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h(q_{i}),h_{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h(q_{i}),h_{q})</annotation></semantics></math>. The idea is to build an <math id="A3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{s}{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{s}{m}</annotation></semantics></math>-ary tree structure to aggregate the information and each query data structure machine is a leaf node of this tree. Recall that each machine <math id="A3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,Q)</annotation></semantics></math> stores the queries <math id="A3.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\{q_{\sigma_{(i-1)\cdot n_{q}+1}},\ldots,q_{\sigma_{i\cdot n_{q}}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\{q_{\sigma_{(i-1)\cdot n_{q}+1}},\ldots,q_{\sigma_{i\cdot n_{q}}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A3.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> contains the start and end of a particular query vector <math id="A3.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A3.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,Q)</annotation></semantics></math> sends a message <math id="A3.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{l},(i,Q))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{l},(i,Q))</annotation></semantics></math> to machine <math id="A3.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h(q_{l}),h_{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h(q_{l}),h_{q})</annotation></semantics></math>. Machine <math id="A3.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,Q)</annotation></semantics></math> also sends the first and last query to its parent machine in the tree, i.e. sends the messages <math id="A3.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{\sigma_{(i-1)\cdot n_{q}+1}},(i,Q),\textup{first})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mtext>first</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{\sigma_{(i-1)\cdot n_{q}+1}},(i,Q),\textup{first})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{\sigma_{i\cdot n_{q}}},(i,Q),\textup{last})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mtext>last</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{\sigma_{i\cdot n_{q}}},(i,Q),\textup{last})</annotation></semantics></math>. After the parent node collects all the messages from the leaf node, it then does the same as its child: if it contains the start and end of a certain query <math id="A3.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, it sends to the location information (the first and last machine that store it) of the query to its corresponding “meta-info” machine <math id="A3.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h(q),h_{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h(q),h_{q})</annotation></semantics></math>, and it sends the first and last query and their location information to its parent machine. This is done recursively, and since there are <math id="A3.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil{mN/s}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil{mN/s}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> query data structure machines in total, the depth of this <math id="A3.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{s}{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{s}{m}</annotation></semantics></math>-ary tree is <math id="A3.p8.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log_{s/m}mN/s)=O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log_{s/m}mN/s)=O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>, which means <math id="A3.p8.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> rounds and <math id="A3.p8.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(mN/s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(mN/s)</annotation></semantics></math> machines suffice.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We do the same for <math id="A3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k,v)</annotation></semantics></math> pairs. The sorting data structure machines <math id="A3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,KV)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,KV)</annotation></semantics></math> sort the (k, v) pairs based on the order of <math id="A3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. As before, we build a <math id="A3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{s}{2m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{s}{2m}</annotation></semantics></math>-ary tree to send the location information to the “meta-info” machine of each key. The different part from query is that we combine the values that have the same key. For each machine in the <math id="A3.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{s}{2m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{s}{2m}</annotation></semantics></math>-ary tree, it computes the averaged value associated with each key it contains and sends the averaged value to the corresponding “meta-info” machine. In particular, for each <math id="A3.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the ‘meta-info” machine for <math id="A3.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h(k_{i}),h_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h(k_{i}),h_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, contains the information <math id="A3.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k_{i},\bar{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k_{i},\bar{v})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A3.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is the average of <math id="A3.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>’s such that <math id="A3.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{j}=k_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{j}=k_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, the “meta-info” machines of query and key need to exchange information to retrieve the corresponding value for each query. Each <math id="A3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,h_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,h_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> sends the <math id="A3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k,\bar{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k,\bar{v})</annotation></semantics></math> pairs it has to the machine <math id="A3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,h_{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,h_{q})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, each <math id="A3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,h_{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,h_{q})</annotation></semantics></math> machine matches the <math id="A3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, and sends the associated value <math id="A3.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{v}</annotation></semantics></math> to the <math id="A3.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that this step can be done by back propagating the <math id="A3.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{s}{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{s}{m}</annotation></semantics></math>-ary tree constructed for sending the location information of <math id="A3.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h(q),h_{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h(q),h_{q})</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, we can just reverse the message sending direction in this tree. Therefore, each query in the query data structure machine receives the value it retrieves and from each query data structure machine <math id="A3.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,Q)</annotation></semantics></math>, we can send the retrieved value for each query to its corresponding token machine, which is the inverse of the second round.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">To summarize, the total rounds needed is <math id="A3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> and the number of machines needed is <math id="A3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(mN/s)=O(N^{1+\varepsilon-\varepsilon^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(mN/s)=O(N^{1+\varepsilon-\varepsilon^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math>. To make this work for <math id="A3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> heads, we can create <math id="A3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> copies of this and each copy runs in parallel. Since <math id="A3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="mH=O(N^{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">mH=O(N^{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>, the bounds for number of rounds and machines still hold. By creating this MPC simulation for each of the <math id="A3.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-layers, we stack them in the order of layers yielding the complete simulation for <math id="A3.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-layer EMA-transformer.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we generalize the above algorithm and proceed to simulate the ANN attention that can be computed by Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.2 Transformer based on Approximate Nearest Neighbor Attention ‣ 3 Approximate Nearest Neighbor Attention ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Since Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.2 Transformer based on Approximate Nearest Neighbor Attention ‣ 3 Approximate Nearest Neighbor Attention ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> is a randomized algorithm, we assume that the MPC protocol shares all the random seeds needed for all the layers of ANNA-transformer.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem C.3</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(MPC simulates ANNA)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix constants <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-layer ANNA-transformer <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> (as implemented by <a href="#alg1" title="In 3.2 Transformer based on Approximate Nearest Neighbor Attention ‣ 3 Approximate Nearest Neighbor Attention ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) with <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="mH=O(N^{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">mH=O(N^{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(L/(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(L/(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon))</annotation></semantics></math>-round MPC protocol <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> with local memory <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=O(N^{1+\varepsilon-\varepsilon^{\prime}+\nicefrac{{3}}{{c^{2}}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded voffset="0.3em"><mn mathsize="0.710em">3</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:-0.15em;" lspace="-0.1em" width="-0.15em"><mo stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo></mpadded><msup><mi mathsize="0.710em">c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=O(N^{1+\varepsilon-\varepsilon^{\prime}+\nicefrac{{3}}{{c^{2}}}})</annotation></semantics></math> machines such that
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(\mathtt{input})=T(\mathtt{input})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\mathtt{input})=T(\mathtt{input})</annotation></semantics></math> for all
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{input}\in\mathbb{Z}_{2^{p}}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚒𝚗𝚙𝚞𝚝</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℤ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msup><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{input}\in\mathbb{Z}_{2^{p}}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">The high level idea of simulating ANNA-transformer is very similar to simulating EMA. We have the same kinds of machines as before. The biggest difference is that, instead of having one hash table for queries and keys, we now have <math id="A3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> hash tables, one for each round of hashing, and we sort the queries and keys based on the hash values of queries and keys.
Again, we first outline different types of machines we will use.</span></p>
<ul id="A3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, machine <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is the <span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">token machine</span> for <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. This machine performs all the element-wise computation for token <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, it computes the query, key, value embeddings <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i},k_{i},v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i},k_{i},v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and element-wise operations after the attention layer.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[\lceil{mN/s}\rceil],t\in[\ell]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[\lceil{mN/s}\rceil],t\in[\ell]</annotation></semantics></math>, machine <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,Q,h^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,Q,h^{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is a data structure machine for sorted queries for the <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th hash table and the <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th chunk of the sorted list of queries, where the ordering of sorting is based on <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}(q)</annotation></semantics></math> from Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.2 Transformer based on Approximate Nearest Neighbor Attention ‣ 3 Approximate Nearest Neighbor Attention ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A3.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\lceil{2mN/s}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\lceil{2mN/s}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>, Machine <math id="A3.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,KV,h^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,KV,h^{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is a data structure machine for sorted list of key and value pairs for the <math id="A3.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th hash table and the <math id="A3.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th chunk of the sorted list of key and value pairs, where the ordering of sorting is based on <math id="A3.I2.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N],t\in[\ell]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N],t\in[\ell]</annotation></semantics></math>, Machine <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g_{t}(q_{i}),h_{q},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g_{t}(q_{i}),h_{q},t)</annotation></semantics></math> is the “meta-info" machine for the queries whose <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th hash value is <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}(q_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}(q_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h_{q_{i}}^{t}=\{q_{j}|j\in[N],g_{t}(q_{j})=g_{t}(q_{i})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{q_{i}}^{t}=\{q_{j}|j\in[N],g_{t}(q_{j})=g_{t}(q_{i})\}</annotation></semantics></math>. This machine stores the location information of <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in h_{q_{i}}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in h_{q_{i}}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in the <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th hash table. Specifically, for all <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in h_{q_{i}}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in h_{q_{i}}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, this machine stores the start machine index, i.e. <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\textup{start},Q,h^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>start</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\textup{start},Q,h^{t})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textup{start}=\argmin_{j}\{q\in" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>start</mtext><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{start}=\argmin_{j}\{q\in</annotation></semantics></math> Machine <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j,Q,h^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j,Q,h^{t})</annotation></semantics></math>}, and the end machine index, i.e. <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\textup{end},Q,h^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>end</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\textup{end},Q,h^{t})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textup{end}=\arg\max_{j}\{q\in" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>end</mtext><mo>=</mo><mi>arg</mi><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{end}=\arg\max_{j}\{q\in</annotation></semantics></math> Machine <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j,Q,h^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j,Q,h^{t})</annotation></semantics></math>}.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N],t\in[\ell]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N],t\in[\ell]</annotation></semantics></math>, Machine <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g_{t}(k_{i}),h_{k},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g_{t}(k_{i}),h_{k},t)</annotation></semantics></math> is the “meta-info" machine for the keys whose <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th hash value is <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}(k_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}(k_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h_{k_{i}}^{t}=\{k_{j}|j\in[N],g_{t}(k_{j})=g_{t}(k_{i})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k_{i}}^{t}=\{k_{j}|j\in[N],g_{t}(k_{j})=g_{t}(k_{i})\}</annotation></semantics></math>. This machine stores the location information of <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in h_{k_{i}}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in h_{k_{i}}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in the <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th hash table. Specifically, for all <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in h_{k_{i}}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in h_{k_{i}}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, this machine stores the start machine index, i.e. <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\textup{start},KV,h^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>start</mtext><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\textup{start},KV,h^{t})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textup{start}=\argmin_{j}\{k\in" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>start</mtext><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{start}=\argmin_{j}\{k\in</annotation></semantics></math> Machine <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j,KV,h^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j,KV,h^{t})</annotation></semantics></math>}, and the end machine index, i.e. <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\textup{end},Q,h^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>end</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\textup{end},Q,h^{t})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textup{end}=\arg\max_{j}\{k\in" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>end</mtext><mo>=</mo><mi>arg</mi><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{end}=\arg\max_{j}\{k\in</annotation></semantics></math> Machine <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j,KV,h^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j,KV,h^{t})</annotation></semantics></math>}.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The auxiliary machines needed for message propagation.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">Like before, we still use each token machine to compute the embeddings <math id="A3.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i},k_{i},v_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i},k_{i},v_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, each token machine need to send <math id="A3.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{i},i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{i},i)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k_{i},v_{i},i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k_{i},v_{i},i)</annotation></semantics></math> to the data structure machines, machine <math id="A3.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lceil{mi/s}\rceil,Q,h^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lceil{mi/s}\rceil,Q,h^{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and machine <math id="A3.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lceil{2mi/s}\rceil,KV,h^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lceil{2mi/s}\rceil,KV,h^{t})</annotation></semantics></math> , for all <math id="A3.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\ell</annotation></semantics></math>. Because <math id="A3.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=N^{3\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=N^{3\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, we use the <math id="A3.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{s}{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{s}{m}</annotation></semantics></math>-ary tree to propagate the queries and keys to the corresponding data structure machines. This takes <math id="A3.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> rounds and <math id="A3.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N^{1+3\rho+\varepsilon-\varepsilon^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N^{1+3\rho+\varepsilon-\varepsilon^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> machines.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, for each query hash table <math id="A3.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[\ell]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[\ell]</annotation></semantics></math>, the data structure machines sort the queries based on the hash value of the queries. Same as Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem C.1 (MPC simulates EMA). ‣ Appendix C MPC can Simulate ANNA-transformer ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, we use the <math id="A3.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{s}{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{s}{m}</annotation></semantics></math>-ary tree to send the location information of each hash bucket to its corresponding “meta-info” machine. For each key, value pair hash table <math id="A3.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[\ell]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[\ell]</annotation></semantics></math>, the data structure machines sort the key, value pairs based on the hash value of the keys. After that, use the <math id="A3.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{s}{2m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{s}{2m}</annotation></semantics></math>-ary tree to propagate the information to the corresponding “meta-info” machine. The difference from the EMA simulation is that each machine in this <math id="A3.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{s}{2m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{s}{2m}</annotation></semantics></math>-ary tree maintains the sum of values whose key has the same hash values instead of the averaged value, and also maintains a count of the number of keys. These can be done in <math id="A3.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> rounds and <math id="A3.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N^{1+3\rho+\varepsilon-\varepsilon^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N^{1+3\rho+\varepsilon-\varepsilon^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> number of machines.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, the key “meta-info” machine send the sum of values and count to the corresponding query “meta-info” machines, i.e. machine <math id="A3.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g_{t}(k_{i}),h_{k},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g_{t}(k_{i}),h_{k},t)</annotation></semantics></math> sends to machine <math id="A3.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g_{t}(q_{i}),h_{q},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g_{t}(q_{i}),h_{q},t)</annotation></semantics></math>. Each query “meta-info” machine then follows the <math id="A3.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{s}{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{s}{m}</annotation></semantics></math>-ary tree, broadcasting the sum of values and counts to the queries in the hash table. finally, each query in the hash table needs to propagate the information back to its original token machine. Since each token machine will receive message from <math id="A3.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=N^{3\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=N^{3\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> machines, we again reverse the <math id="A3.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{s}{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{s}{m}</annotation></semantics></math>-ary tree that send the query to each data structure machine. During the aggregation, each machine in the <math id="A3.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{s}{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{s}{m}</annotation></semantics></math>-ary tree still maintains the sum of values and the sum of counts it receives. After receiving the sum of values and counts, each token machine <math id="A3.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> then calculates <math id="A3.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{ANNA}(q_{i})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>ANNA</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{ANNA}(q_{i})=</annotation></semantics></math> sum of the values divided by the counts.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">The above simulates one layer of ANNA-transformer in <math id="A3.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> rounds and using <math id="A3.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N^{1+3\rho+\varepsilon-\varepsilon^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N^{1+3\rho+\varepsilon-\varepsilon^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> machines, where <math id="A3.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1/c^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1/c^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, by stacking the simulation for <math id="A3.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> layers, this gives <math id="A3.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{L}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{L}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> rounds in total. To extend to <math id="A3.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> heads, we just need to instantiate the above simulation for <math id="A3.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> parallel copies and because <math id="A3.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="mH=O(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">mH=O(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, the total number of rounds and machines still remains the same.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>ANN/EM Attention can simulate low-rank Attention via MPC</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We simulate the low-rank attention using ANN attention by first giving a MPC algorithm for computing low-rank attention and then convert it to ANNA-transformer.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(ANNA/EMA simulates low-rank Attention)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For constants <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, any low-rank attention based transformer with depth <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, rank <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, embedding dimension <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rm=O(N^{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rm=O(N^{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> can be simulated by an EMA/ANNA-transformer with depth <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{L}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{L}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>, number of heads <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> and embedding dimension <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(N^{5\varepsilon^{\prime}}\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(N^{5\varepsilon^{\prime}}\log N)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove this theorem by first proving that any one-layer of low-rank attention can simulated by constant number of rounds of MPC.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(MPC simulates low-rank Attention)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For constants <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, any one-layer low-rank attention with rank <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, embedding dimension <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rm=O(N^{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rm=O(N^{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> can be simulated by a <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>-round MPC protocol with local memory <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N)</annotation></semantics></math> machines.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume <math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rm=O(N^{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rm=O(N^{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> and local memory of MPC <math id="A4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Same as what we do in MPC simulating EMA, for each token <math id="A4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i},i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i},i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have a token machine <math id="A4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> to compute the embedding of <math id="A4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> but we need to compute it in the kernel space, i.e. <math id="A4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=Q^{\prime}(x_{i}),k_{i}=K^{\prime}(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=Q^{\prime}(x_{i}),k_{i}=K^{\prime}(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}=V(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}=V(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. To compute <math id="A4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}(X)^{{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}}V(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}(X)^{{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}}V(X)</annotation></semantics></math>, recall that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}(X)^{{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}}V(X)=\sum_{i=1}^{N}k_{i}v_{i}^{{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}(X)^{{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}}V(X)=\sum_{i=1}^{N}k_{i}v_{i}^{{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">We just need to compute the sum of <math id="A4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> matrices of size <math id="A4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\times m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\times m</annotation></semantics></math>. Each token machine <math id="A4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> computes the matrix <math id="A4.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{i}v_{i}^{{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{i}v_{i}^{{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and we construct a <math id="A4.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lfloor{\frac{s}{rm}}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lfloor{\frac{s}{rm}}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>-ary tree of machines to compute the sum. The leaves of the tree are all the token machines and each node is responsible for computing the sum of <math id="A4.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lfloor{\frac{s}{rm}}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lfloor{\frac{s}{rm}}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math> number of matrices. We know from the previous simulation that the depth of the tree is <math id="A4.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>. After we obtain the matrix <math id="A4.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=K^{\prime}(X)^{{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}}V(X)\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=K^{\prime}(X)^{{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}}V(X)\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>, in order to compute <math id="A4.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(X)K^{\prime}(X)^{{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}}V(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(X)K^{\prime}(X)^{{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}}V(X)</annotation></semantics></math>, we just need to propagate the matrix <math id="A4.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> to all the token machines. And each token machine <math id="A4.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> computes <math id="A4.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}^{{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}}M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}^{{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}}M</annotation></semantics></math>. By reversing the direction of message propagation in the computing sum tree, we can propagate <math id="A4.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> to all the token machines in <math id="A4.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> rounds. Therefore, we can simulate kernel attention with <math id="A4.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> rounds in total.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> layers of low-rank attention transformer, we construct the MPC for each layer using Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2 (MPC simulates low-rank Attention). ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix D ANN/EM Attention can simulate low-rank Attention via MPC ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> and again we use the local computation of each token machine to simulate the element-wise computation. We stack the <math id="A4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> MPCs together, which has <math id="A4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{L}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{L}{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> rounds. The theorem follows from applying Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem B.2 (EMA simulates MPC). ‣ Appendix B ANNA-transformer can simulate MPC ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> and Corollary <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem9" title="Corollary B.9 (ANNA simulates MPC). ‣ Appendix B ANNA-transformer can simulate MPC ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.9</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Since the core of the proof is through MPC simulating low-rank Attention, we can also apply Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem10" title="Theorem B.10 (EMA simulates MPC with improved embedding dimension). ‣ Appendix B ANNA-transformer can simulate MPC ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.10</span></a> and Corollary <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem14" title="Corollary B.14 (ANNA simulates MPC with improved embedding dimension). ‣ Appendix B ANNA-transformer can simulate MPC ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.14</span></a> which simulate MPC with better embedding dimension to get a improved embedding dimension for simulating low-rank attention transformer.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary D.3</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(ANNA/EMA simulates low-rank Attention with improved embedding dimension)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For constants <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, any low-rank attention based transformer with depth <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, rank <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, embedding dimension <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rm=O(N^{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rm=O(N^{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> can be simulated by an EMA/ANNA-transformer with depth <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{L}{(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)\cdot\min(\varepsilon^{2},(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)^{2})})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{L}{(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)\cdot\min(\varepsilon^{2},(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)^{2})})</annotation></semantics></math>, number of heads <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=O(N^{\frac{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon}{4}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=O(N^{\frac{\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon}{4}})</annotation></semantics></math> and embedding dimension <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Discussion on Reformer</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We formally define Reformer as a computational model here.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Reformer attention)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given query, key, value embeddings <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(X),K(X),V(X)\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(X),K(X),V(X)\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times m}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{i}:=k_{i}=Q(X)[i,:]=K(X)[i,:],v_{i}=V(X)[i,:]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}:=k_{i}=Q(X)[i,:]=K(X)[i,:],v_{i}=V(X)[i,:]</annotation></semantics></math>, <em id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">Reformer</em> attention proceeds as follows:</span></p>
<ol id="A5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Apply a hash function </span><math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:\mathbb{R}^{m}\rightarrow U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:\mathbb{R}^{m}\rightarrow U</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> on </span><math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{q_{1},\ldots,q_{N}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{q_{1},\ldots,q_{N}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Sort all </span><math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">’s (and thus </span><math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">’s) by </span><math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(q_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(q_{i})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and partition all </span><math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">’s into chunks of size </span><math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\leq O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\leq O(1)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and let </span><math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\prime}(q_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\prime}(q_{i})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be the label of the chunk that </span><math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is in (the queries in each chunk can have different hash values);</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each </span><math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, only attend to </span><math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{j}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">’s such that they are in the same chunk.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The output embedding for <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is therefore</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{j:h^{\prime}(k_{j})=h^{\prime}(q_{i})}\frac{\exp(\langle q_{i},k_{j}\rangle)}{\displaystyle\sum_{j^{\prime}:h^{\prime}(k_{j^{\prime}})=h^{\prime}(q_{i})}\exp(\langle q_{i},k_{j^{\prime}}\rangle)}\cdot v_{j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j:h^{\prime}(k_{j})=h^{\prime}(q_{i})}\frac{\exp(\langle q_{i},k_{j}\rangle)}{\displaystyle\sum_{j^{\prime}:h^{\prime}(k_{j^{\prime}})=h^{\prime}(q_{i})}\exp(\langle q_{i},k_{j^{\prime}}\rangle)}\cdot v_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We define <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\ell}:[N]\rightarrow[N]^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>B</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\ell}:[N]\rightarrow[N]^{B}</annotation></semantics></math> as the function that specifies the set of keys each query should compute inner product with in the <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer. From the Reformer constraints, we have <math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ol id="A5.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\ell}(i)=\{a_{1},a_{2},\ldots,a_{B}\}\in[N]^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>B</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\ell}(i)=\{a_{1},a_{2},\ldots,a_{B}\}\in[N]^{B}</annotation></semantics></math> is a set (no repetition).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in f_{\ell}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in f_{\ell}(i)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in f_{\ell}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in f_{\ell}(i)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\ell}(j)=f_{\ell}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\ell}(j)=f_{\ell}(i)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">In the <math id="A5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer attention computation for each query <math id="A5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, Reformer computes</p>
<table id="A5.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\in f_{\ell}(i)}\frac{\exp(\langle q_{i},k_{j}\rangle)}{\displaystyle\sum_{j^{\prime}\in f_{\ell}(i)}\exp(\langle q_{i},k_{j^{\prime}}\rangle)}\cdot v_{j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\in f_{\ell}(i)}\frac{\exp(\langle q_{i},k_{j}\rangle)}{\displaystyle\sum_{j^{\prime}\in f_{\ell}(i)}\exp(\langle q_{i},k_{j^{\prime}}\rangle)}\cdot v_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We first study a restricted version of Reformer that fix the communication pattern beforehand i.e. <math id="A5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is input-independent for all <math id="A5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[L]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[L]</annotation></semantics></math>, and show that it can not compute the sum of all the input tokens.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition E.2</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(SUM)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given input <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=(x_{1},x_{2},\ldots,x_{N}),x_{i}\in[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=(x_{1},x_{2},\ldots,x_{N}),x_{i}\in[M]</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=N^{O(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=N^{O(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, the </span>SUM<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> task is defined as <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{SUM}(X)=\sum_{i=1}^{N}x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>SUM</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{SUM}(X)=\sum_{i=1}^{N}x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We say a Reformer <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> computes </span>SUM<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> if for all <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(X)_{N}=\textup{SUM}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>SUM</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(X)_{N}=\textup{SUM}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(X)_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(X)_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>-th output of T given the input <math id="A5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. One can choose any position to be the final output position, and here WLOG we choose the last token to follow the autoregressive generation model convention.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition E.3</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{f_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{f_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>. Any Reformer <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> layers and each layer the attention pattern is specified by <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{f_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{f_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> can not compute <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{SUM}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>SUM</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{SUM}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>: there exists an <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|T(X)_{N}-\textup{SUM}(X)|\geq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>SUM</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|T(X)_{N}-\textup{SUM}(X)|\geq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\epsilon&lt;M/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\epsilon&lt;M/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We denote each layer’s element-wise computation by <math id="A5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\phi_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\phi_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\ell}(X)_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\ell}(X)_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <math id="A5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th output of <math id="A5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> after <math id="A5.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> layers of computation. We prove this proposition by induction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Inductive hypothesis: <math id="A5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\ell}(X)_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\ell}(X)_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a function of at most <math id="A5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> different <math id="A5.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}\in X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}\in X</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Base case: <math id="A5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=1</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T^{1}(X)_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T^{1}(X)_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j\in f_{1}(i)}\frac{\exp(\langle q_{i},k_{j}\rangle)}{\displaystyle\sum_{j^{\prime}\in f_{1}(i)}\exp(\langle q_{i},k_{j^{\prime}}\rangle)}\cdot v_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j\in f_{1}(i)}\frac{\exp(\langle q_{i},k_{j}\rangle)}{\displaystyle\sum_{j^{\prime}\in f_{1}(i)}\exp(\langle q_{i},k_{j^{\prime}}\rangle)}\cdot v_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j\in f_{1}(i)}\frac{\exp(\langle Q(x_{i}),K(x_{j})\rangle)}{\displaystyle\sum_{j^{\prime}\in f_{1}(i)}\exp(\langle Q(x_{i}),K(x_{j^{\prime}})\rangle)}\cdot V(x_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j\in f_{1}(i)}\frac{\exp(\langle Q(x_{i}),K(x_{j})\rangle)}{\displaystyle\sum_{j^{\prime}\in f_{1}(i)}\exp(\langle Q(x_{i}),K(x_{j^{\prime}})\rangle)}\cdot V(x_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\phi_{1}(x_{a_{1}},x_{a_{2}},\ldots,x_{a_{B}})\;\text{where}f_{1}(i)=\{a_{1},\ldots,a_{B}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>where</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\phi_{1}(x_{a_{1}},x_{a_{2}},\ldots,x_{a_{B}})\;\text{where}f_{1}(i)=\{a_{1},\ldots,a_{B}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">which is a function of at most <math id="A5.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A5.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s in <math id="A5.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Inductive step: consider</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T^{\ell+1}(X)_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T^{\ell+1}(X)_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j\in f_{\ell+1}(i)}\frac{\exp(\langle Q(T^{\ell}(X)_{i}),K(T^{\ell}(X)_{j})\rangle)}{\displaystyle\sum_{j^{\prime}\in f_{\ell+1}(i)}\exp(\langle Q(T^{\ell}(X)_{i}),K(T^{\ell}(X)_{j^{\prime}})\rangle)}\cdot V(T^{\ell}(X)_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j\in f_{\ell+1}(i)}\frac{\exp(\langle Q(T^{\ell}(X)_{i}),K(T^{\ell}(X)_{j})\rangle)}{\displaystyle\sum_{j^{\prime}\in f_{\ell+1}(i)}\exp(\langle Q(T^{\ell}(X)_{i}),K(T^{\ell}(X)_{j^{\prime}})\rangle)}\cdot V(T^{\ell}(X)_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\phi_{\ell+1}(T^{\ell}(X)_{a_{1}},\ldots,T^{\ell}(X)_{a_{B}})\;\text{where}f_{1}(i)=\{a_{1},\ldots,a_{B}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>where</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\phi_{\ell+1}(T^{\ell}(X)_{a_{1}},\ldots,T^{\ell}(X)_{a_{B}})\;\text{where}f_{1}(i)=\{a_{1},\ldots,a_{B}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since each <math id="A5.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\ell}(X)_{a_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\ell}(X)_{a_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a function of at most <math id="A5.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> variables from <math id="A5.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\ell+1}(X)_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\ell+1}(X)_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a function of at most <math id="A5.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\cdot B^{\ell}=B^{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\cdot B^{\ell}=B^{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math> variables from <math id="A5.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, if <math id="A5.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{L}(X)_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{L}(X)_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a function of all <math id="A5.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{1},\ldots,x_{N}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{1},\ldots,x_{N}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we need <math id="A5.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{L}\geq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{L}\geq N</annotation></semantics></math> and thus <math id="A5.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=\Omega(\log_{B}N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=\Omega(\log_{B}N)</annotation></semantics></math>. In the case <math id="A5.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{L}(X)_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{L}(X)_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a function of <math id="A5.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{L}\ll N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>≪</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{L}\ll N</annotation></semantics></math> variables. WLOG, consider <math id="A5.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{L}(X)_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{L}(X)_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is a function of <math id="A5.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{1},\ldots,x_{B^{L}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{1},\ldots,x_{B^{L}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, <math id="A5.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{B^{L}+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{B^{L}+1}</annotation></semantics></math> can be any number in <math id="A5.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[M]</annotation></semantics></math> that makes <math id="A5.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{L}(X)_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{L}(X)_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> far from <math id="A5.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{SUM}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>SUM</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{SUM}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, if Reformer has any power, it must come from the sorting part, because the sorting algorithm have access to the information of all the token inputs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Although constant-layer Reformer can not compute SUM, one can easily show that one layer of ANNA-transformer can compute SUM by setting <math id="A5.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}=Nx_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}=Nx_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1}=k_{2}=\cdots=k_{N}=q_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1}=k_{2}=\cdots=k_{N}=q_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A5.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, thereby retrieving all the <math id="A5.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s and averaging them.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>ANNA-transformer Solves <math id="A6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-hop and <span id="A6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Match2</span></h2>

<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>ANNA/EMA-transformer Solves <span id="A6.SS1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Match2</span></h3>

<div id="A6.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem F.1</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N,M=N^{O(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N,M=N^{O(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists an EMA-transformer <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> with one layer, one attention head, and embedding dimension <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(X)=\textup{Match2}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Match2</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(X)=\textup{Match2}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in[M]^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in[M]^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Given input <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in[0,M]^{N\times 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in[0,M]^{N\times 1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(X)=\phi(X)Q,K(X)=\phi(X)K,V(X)=\phi(X)V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(X)=\phi(X)Q,K(X)=\phi(X)K,V(X)=\phi(X)V</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K,V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K,V</annotation></semantics></math> are matrices in <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{2\times 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{2\times 1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x)=(x,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x)=(x,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\begin{pmatrix}1\\
0\end{pmatrix},K=\begin{pmatrix}-1\\
M\end{pmatrix},V=\begin{pmatrix}0\\
1\end{pmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>M</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\begin{pmatrix}1\\
0\end{pmatrix},K=\begin{pmatrix}-1\\
M\end{pmatrix},V=\begin{pmatrix}0\\
1\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">such that</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(X)Q=\begin{pmatrix}x_{1}\\
x_{2}\\
\vdots\\
x_{N}\end{pmatrix},\phi(X)K=\begin{pmatrix}M-x_{1}\\
M-x_{2}\\
\vdots\\
M-x_{N}\end{pmatrix},\phi(X)V=\begin{pmatrix}1\\
1\\
\vdots\\
1\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(X)Q=\begin{pmatrix}x_{1}\\
x_{2}\\
\vdots\\
x_{N}\end{pmatrix},\phi(X)K=\begin{pmatrix}M-x_{1}\\
M-x_{2}\\
\vdots\\
M-x_{N}\end{pmatrix},\phi(X)V=\begin{pmatrix}1\\
1\\
\vdots\\
1\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">As a result, for each <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq N</annotation></semantics></math>, if there exists <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq j\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq j\leq N</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}+x_{j}=M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}+x_{j}=M</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="((\phi(X)Q)(\phi(X)K)^{{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}})[i,j]=\frac{1}{|\{j\in[N]:x_{i}+x_{j}=M\}|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">((\phi(X)Q)(\phi(X)K)^{{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}})[i,j]=\frac{1}{|\{j\in[N]:x_{i}+x_{j}=M\}|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Otherwise, <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="((\phi(X)Q)(\phi(X)K)^{{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}})[i,j]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">((\phi(X)Q)(\phi(X)K)^{{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}})[i,j]=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq j\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq j\leq N</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, we can calculate that if <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\{j\in[N]:x_{i}+x_{j}=M\}|\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{j\in[N]:x_{i}+x_{j}=M\}|\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textup{EMA}(\phi(X)Q,\phi(X)K,\phi(X)V)[i]=\frac{1}{|\{j\in[N]:x_{i}+x_{j}=M\}|}\cdot|\{j\in[N]:x_{i}+x_{j}=M\}|=1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>EMA</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{EMA}(\phi(X)Q,\phi(X)K,\phi(X)V)[i]=\frac{1}{|\{j\in[N]:x_{i}+x_{j}=M\}|}\cdot|\{j\in[N]:x_{i}+x_{j}=M\}|=1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">and if <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\{j\in[N]:x_{i}+x_{j}=M\}|=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{j\in[N]:x_{i}+x_{j}=M\}|=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{EMA}(\phi(X)Q,\phi(X)K,\phi(X)V)[i]=0.\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>EMA</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{EMA}(\phi(X)Q,\phi(X)K,\phi(X)V)[i]=0.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">That gives the same result for ANNA-transformers.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary F.2</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N,M=N^{O(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N,M=N^{O(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists an ANNA-transformer <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> with one layer, one attention head, and embedding dimension <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(X)=\textup{Match2}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Match2</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(X)=\textup{Match2}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in[M]^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in[M]^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>ANN transformer Solves <math id="A6.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-hop</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first show that ANNA transformers can solve induction head (<math id="A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-hop).</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma F.3</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix constants <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Sigma|\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Sigma|\leq N</annotation></semantics></math>.
There exists an ANNA-transformer <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon\cdot(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)^{2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon\cdot(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)^{2}})</annotation></semantics></math> layers, <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=O(N^{(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)/4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=O(N^{(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)/4})</annotation></semantics></math> heads per layer, and embedding dimension <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(w)_{i}=w_{\sigma(w,i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(w)_{i}=w_{\sigma(w,i)}</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(w,i)\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(w,i)\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T(w)_{i}=\bot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">⊥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(w)_{i}=\bot</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(w,i)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(w,i)=0</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in\Sigma^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in\Sigma^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove this lemma by designing a constant-round MPC algorithm with local memory <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=O(N^{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=O(N^{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N/s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N/s</annotation></semantics></math> machines to solve <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-hop. Since <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Sigma|\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Sigma|\leq N</annotation></semantics></math>, each token can be embedded with <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log N)</annotation></semantics></math> bits (<math id="A6.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> words). Denote the input <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{N}=(x_{1},x_{2},\ldots,x_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{N}=(x_{1},x_{2},\ldots,x_{N})</annotation></semantics></math>. The MPC algorithm works as following:</span></p>
<ol id="A6.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, retrieve the next token <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and each token on the machine is stored as the embedding of <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i},i,x_{i+1},i+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i},i,x_{i+1},i+1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define a comparator <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math> for the object <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i},i,x_{i+1},i+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i},i,x_{i+1},i+1)</annotation></semantics></math>. For two tuples <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i},i,x_{i+1},i+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i},i,x_{i+1},i+1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{j},j,x_{j+1},j+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{j},j,x_{j+1},j+1)</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}\neq x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}\neq x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}&lt;x_{j}\Rightarrow(x_{i},i,x_{i+1},i+1)&lt;(x_{j},j,x_{j+1},j+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}&lt;x_{j}\Rightarrow(x_{i},i,x_{i+1},i+1)&lt;(x_{j},j,x_{j+1},j+1)</annotation></semantics></math>; if <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}=x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}=x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;j\Rightarrow(x_{i},i,x_{i+1},i+1)&lt;(x_{j},j,x_{j+1},j+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;j\Rightarrow(x_{i},i,x_{i+1},i+1)&lt;(x_{j},j,x_{j+1},j+1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Sort <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i},i,x_{i+1},i+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i},i,x_{i+1},i+1)</annotation></semantics></math> by the comparator <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each token <math id="A6.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i},i,x_{i+1},i+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i},i,x_{i+1},i+1)</annotation></semantics></math> in the sorted list retrieves the token before it in the sorted list, denoted by <math id="A6.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{j},j,x_{j+1},j+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{j},j,x_{j+1},j+1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Update the embedding of token: if <math id="A6.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}=x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}=x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the embedding of the token <math id="A6.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes <math id="A6.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,x_{j+1},j+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,x_{j+1},j+1)</annotation></semantics></math> i.e. <math id="A6.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,w_{\sigma(w,i)},\sigma(w,i))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,w_{\sigma(w,i)},\sigma(w,i))</annotation></semantics></math>; if <math id="A6.I1.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{j}\neq w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{j}\neq w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the embedding of the token <math id="A6.I1.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes <math id="A6.I1.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,\bot,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⊥</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,\bot,0)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Send each <math id="A6.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,w_{\sigma(w,i)},\sigma(w,i))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,w_{\sigma(w,i)},\sigma(w,i))</annotation></semantics></math> to the correct output machine <math id="A6.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil{\frac{i}{s}}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil{\frac{i}{s}}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> and output <math id="A6.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\sigma(w,i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\sigma(w,i)}</annotation></semantics></math> for token <math id="A6.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">For step 1, each machine only needs to send message to its neighbor machine: machine <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> sends message to machine <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i-1</annotation></semantics></math>, and this only takes 1 round. In step 2, each tuple is only <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log N)</annotation></semantics></math> bits, so by <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma C.2 (MPC Sorting). ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix C MPC can Simulate ANNA-transformer ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>, the sorting takes <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> rounds. In step 3, again each machine only needs to send message to its neighbor machine: machine <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> sends message to machine <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i+1</annotation></semantics></math>, and this only takes 1 round. In step 4, each machine for the sorted list sends at most <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> tuples stored in it to the correct output machine which takes 1 round. Thus, the MPC algorithm has <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> rounds in total.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we convert this MPC algorithm to an ANNA-transformer. By <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem14" title="Corollary B.14 (ANNA simulates MPC with improved embedding dimension). ‣ Appendix B ANNA-transformer can simulate MPC ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.14</span></a>, this gives us an ANNA-transformer with number of heads <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=O(N^{(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)/4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=O(N^{(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)/4})</annotation></semantics></math>, embedding dimension <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> and number of layers <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon\cdot(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)^{2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon\cdot(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)^{2}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now we show that ANNA-transformers can solve <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-hop with <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log k)</annotation></semantics></math> layers.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem F.4</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix constants <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\varepsilon^{\prime}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Sigma|\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Sigma|\leq N</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.
There exists an ANNA-transformer <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=O\left(\frac{1}{\varepsilon\cdot(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)^{2}}+\frac{\log k}{(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)^{2}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=O\left(\frac{1}{\varepsilon\cdot(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)^{2}}+\frac{\log k}{(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> layers, <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=O(N^{(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)/4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=O(N^{(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)/4})</annotation></semantics></math> heads per layer, and embedding dimension <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(w)_{i}=w_{\sigma^{k}(w,i)},\forall i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(w)_{i}=w_{\sigma^{k}(w,i)},\forall i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in\Sigma^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in\Sigma^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove this theorem by constructing an <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log k)</annotation></semantics></math>-rounds MPC with <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=O(N^{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=O(N^{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> local memory and <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N/s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N/s)</annotation></semantics></math> machines. We show that this MPC algorithm can compute <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-hop by induction. Let <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=\sum_{j=0}^{\lfloor\log k\rfloor}k_{j}2^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\sum_{j=0}^{\lfloor\log k\rfloor}k_{j}2^{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="k_{:\ell}=\sum_{j=0}^{\ell-1}k_{j}2^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>k</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{:\ell}=\sum_{j=0}^{\ell-1}k_{j}2^{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{j}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{j}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Inductive hypothesis: after <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon})+2\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon})+2\ell</annotation></semantics></math> rounds of MPC computation, the token embedding for each token <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> encodes the information of this tuple</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(i,w_{\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i)},\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i),w_{\sigma^{k_{:\ell}}(w,i)},\sigma^{k_{:\ell}}(w,i))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,w_{\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i)},\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i),w_{\sigma^{k_{:\ell}}(w,i)},\sigma^{k_{:\ell}}(w,i))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Base case: <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=0,k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=0,k=1</annotation></semantics></math> is implied by <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma F.3. ‣ F.2 ANN transformer Solves 𝑘-hop ‣ Appendix F ANNA-transformer Solves 𝑘-hop and Match2 ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a>. After step 3, we have <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,w_{\sigma(w,i)},\sigma(w,i))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,w_{\sigma(w,i)},\sigma(w,i))</annotation></semantics></math>.
Now consider <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=\ell+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\ell+1</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, the machine (Machine <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil{i/s}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil{i/s}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>) that contains <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(i,w_{\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i)},\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i),w_{\sigma^{k_{:\ell}}(w,i)},\sigma^{k_{:\ell}}(w,i))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,w_{\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i)},\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i),w_{\sigma^{k_{:\ell}}(w,i)},\sigma^{k_{:\ell}}(w,i))</annotation></semantics></math> sends the message <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i))</annotation></semantics></math> to machine that contains <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i)</annotation></semantics></math> as the first entry of the tuple which is machine <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil{\frac{\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i)}{s}}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil{\frac{\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i)}{s}}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>. Machine <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil{\frac{\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i)}{s}}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil{\frac{\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i)}{s}}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> then send the following tuple to machine <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil{i/s}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil{i/s}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle(\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i),w_{\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i))},\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i)),w_{\sigma^{k_{:\ell}}(w,\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i))},\sigma^{k_{:\ell}}(w,\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i),w_{\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i))},\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i)),w_{\sigma^{k_{:\ell}}(w,\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i))},\sigma^{k_{:\ell}}(w,\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i)))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=(\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i),w_{\sigma^{2^{\ell+1}}(w,i)},\sigma^{2^{\ell+1}}(w,i),w_{\sigma^{k_{:\ell}+2^{\ell}}(w,i)},\sigma^{k_{:\ell}+2^{\ell}}(w,i))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i),w_{\sigma^{2^{\ell+1}}(w,i)},\sigma^{2^{\ell+1}}(w,i),w_{\sigma^{k_{:\ell}+2^{\ell}}(w,i)},\sigma^{k_{:\ell}+2^{\ell}}(w,i))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=(\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i),t_{1},t_{2},t_{3},t_{4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=(\sigma^{2^{\ell}}(w,i),t_{1},t_{2},t_{3},t_{4})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since each machine has at most <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> tuples and the function <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(w,i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(w,i)</annotation></semantics></math> is one-to-one except for <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bot</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of messages each machine sends and receive is bounded by <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>. After machine <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil{i/s}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil{i/s}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> receiving the above message, it update the tuple for the token <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<ol id="A6.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A6.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">if <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\ell}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\ell}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, token <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is updated as: <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(i,t_{1},t_{2},w_{\sigma^{k_{:\ell}}(w,i)},\sigma^{k_{:\ell}}(w,i))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,t_{1},t_{2},w_{\sigma^{k_{:\ell}}(w,i)},\sigma^{k_{:\ell}}(w,i))</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">if <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\ell}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\ell}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, token <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is updated as: <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,t_{1},t_{2},t_{3},t_{4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,t_{1},t_{2},t_{3},t_{4})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A6.SS2.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">By definition, the embedding of token <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> now is:</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(i,w_{\sigma^{2^{\ell+1}}(w,i)},\sigma^{2^{\ell+1}}(w,i),w_{\sigma^{k_{:\ell+1}}(w,i)},\sigma^{k_{:\ell+1}}(w,i))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,w_{\sigma^{2^{\ell+1}}(w,i)},\sigma^{2^{\ell+1}}(w,i),w_{\sigma^{k_{:\ell+1}}(w,i)},\sigma^{k_{:\ell+1}}(w,i))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">The above inductive step only takes 2 rounds of MPC. Therefore, the total round is <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon})+2(\ell+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon})+2(\ell+1)</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=\lfloor\log k\rfloor+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=\lfloor\log k\rfloor+1</annotation></semantics></math>, this algorithm compute the output for <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-hop.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Again, we can convert this MPC algorithm to an ANNA-transformer. By <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem14" title="Corollary B.14 (ANNA simulates MPC with improved embedding dimension). ‣ Appendix B ANNA-transformer can simulate MPC ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.14</span></a>, this gives us an ANNA-transformer with number of heads <math id="A6.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=O(N^{(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)/4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=O(N^{(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)/4})</annotation></semantics></math>, embedding dimension <math id="A6.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=O(N^{\varepsilon^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> and number of layers <math id="A6.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon\cdot(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)^{2}}+\frac{\log k}{(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)^{2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=O(\frac{1}{\varepsilon\cdot(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)^{2}}+\frac{\log k}{(\varepsilon^{\prime}-\varepsilon)^{2}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Experimental details</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here are the details of the experimental setup. All the experiments are launched on 2 GPUs: NIVIDIA Titan RTX and NVIDIA Titan Xp.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We train a modified version of the attention matrix and then distill from the trained model using ANNA implemented by the angular distance LSH family from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Andoni et al. (2015)</a></cite>. Our softmax attention normalizes all the queries and keys in <math id="A7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(X)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(X)</annotation></semantics></math> to have unit norm, and computes <math id="A7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{softmax}(\beta\cdot Q(X)K(X)^{{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}})V(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝖳</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{softmax}(\beta\cdot Q(X)K(X)^{{\scriptscriptstyle{\mathsf{T}}}})V(X)</annotation></semantics></math> with a hyperparameter <math id="A7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.1 </span>Match2 experiments</h3>

<section id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dataset generation.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Inspired by the way <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kozachinskiy et al. (2025)</a></cite> generating data for Match3 task, a triple-wise version of Match2, we generate the data for Match2 using the same algorithm but change to pair-wise relation when computing the label. Each sample is a tuple <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Y)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=(x_{1},x_{2},\ldots,x_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=(x_{1},x_{2},\ldots,x_{N})</annotation></semantics></math>, and each <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is an integer sampled from <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,2,\ldots,36\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>36</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,2,\ldots,36\}</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=(y_{1},y_{2},\ldots,y_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=(y_{1},y_{2},\ldots,y_{N})</annotation></semantics></math>, and each <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{i}=\mathbbm{1}\{\exists j\centerdot x_{i}+x_{j}=0\bmod 37\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∙</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>mod</mo><mn>37</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}=\mathbbm{1}\{\exists j\centerdot x_{i}+x_{j}=0\bmod 37\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The sequence length <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is set to <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32</annotation></semantics></math>. When sampling the data, we ensure that each batch is balanced by having the distribution of one’s in <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> the same: each batch has <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> bins and each bin corresponds to each percentage <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,25\%),[25\%,50\%),[50\%,75\%),[75\%,100\%]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>25</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>25</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>75</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>75</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,25\%),[25\%,50\%),[50\%,75\%),[75\%,100\%]</annotation></semantics></math> of one’s in <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>; each bin size is <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/4</annotation></semantics></math> of the batch size. See <a href="#alg3" title="In Dataset generation. ‣ G.1 Match2 experiments ‣ Appendix G Experimental details ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> for details.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg3" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span> Match2 Dataset Generation</figcaption>
<div id="alg3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg3.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
                
                
              <math id="alg3.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=32</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg3.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=37" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>37</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=37</annotation></semantics></math>, dataset size <math id="alg3.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
                
                
              Dataset of <math id="alg3.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Y)</annotation></semantics></math> pairs

</div>
<div id="alg3.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
                
                
              Initialize 4 empty bins for ones-percentage ranges: <math id="alg3.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,25)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>25</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,25)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg3.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[25,50)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[25,50)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg3.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[50,75)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>75</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[50,75)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg3.l3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[75,100]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>75,100</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[75,100]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
                
                
              <math id="alg3.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{b}\leftarrow D/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{b}\leftarrow D/4</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg3.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> total examples in bins <math id="alg3.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;D/40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;D/40</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
                
                
                Sample <math id="alg3.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\{1,\ldots,M\}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\{1,\ldots,M\}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly at random

</div>
<div id="alg3.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
                
                
                Calculate the percentage <math id="alg3.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> of one’s in <math id="alg3.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
                
                
                <span id="alg3.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> size of the bin <math id="alg3.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is in <math id="alg3.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;N_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;N_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
                
                
                 Add <math id="alg3.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Y)</annotation></semantics></math> to the correct bin
  
</div>
<div id="alg3.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg3.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each bin <span id="alg3.l10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
                
                
                <span id="alg3.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> size of bin <math id="alg3.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;N_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;N_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
                
                
                 Randomly sample <math id="alg3.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Y)</annotation></semantics></math> from bin

</div>
<div id="alg3.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
                
                
                 Sample permutation <math id="alg3.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="alg3.l13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,\ldots,N-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\ldots,N-1]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
                
                
                 <math id="alg3.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\ast}\leftarrow X[\pi]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\ast}\leftarrow X[\pi]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg3.l14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{\ast}\leftarrow Y[\pi]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{\ast}\leftarrow Y[\pi]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
                
                
                 Add <math id="alg3.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X^{\ast},Y^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X^{\ast},Y^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> to bin

</div>
<div id="alg3.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
                
                
              Combine and shuffle all bins into final dataset

</div>
<div id="alg3.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg3.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> Dataset

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training details.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We trained <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> models with <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in\{0.1,1,10\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in\{0.1,1,10\}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively, with Adam optimizer on cross-entropy loss and learning rate <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math>. Each model has one layer, one attention head, embedding dimension <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=64</annotation></semantics></math> and an MLP with width <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4m</annotation></semantics></math> and GeLU activation. The dataset size, batch size, training steps are <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10000,32,20000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10000</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>20000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10000,32,20000</annotation></semantics></math> respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We apply ANNA with number of hash tables <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\{1,2,\ldots,16\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\{1,2,\ldots,16\}</annotation></semantics></math> and number of hash functions for each table <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\{1,2,\ldots,6\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\{1,2,\ldots,6\}</annotation></semantics></math> on all the <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> trained models, and <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> has the best performance (error can be <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>). Since the implementation of ANNA is randomized, for each combination of <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\ell,z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\ell,z)</annotation></semantics></math>, we run <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> times and report the averaged error over the <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> runs. See <a href="#S5.F1.sf1" title="In Figure 1 ‣ 5.3 Experiments on Match2 and induction heads ‣ 5 ANNA-transformer for reasoning tasks ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1(a)</span></a> for plotted performance when <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>. In this setting, <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\geq 8,z=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\geq 8,z=1</annotation></semantics></math> can achieve <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> error on the test set with <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>256</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256</annotation></semantics></math> test samples.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.2 </span>Induction heads experiments</h3>

<section id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dataset generation.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the data generation algorithm from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sanford et al. (2024c)</a></cite>. Each sample <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Y)</annotation></semantics></math> is of the form <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=(k,X^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=(k,X^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> for training samples and <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math> for test samples, <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}\in\Sigma^{N-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}\in\Sigma^{N-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=(0,Y^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=(0,Y^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-hop label for <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Here the sequence length <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=100</annotation></semantics></math> and alphabet size <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Sigma|=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Sigma|=4</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training details.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We trained <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> models with <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in\{0.1,1,10\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in\{0.1,1,10\}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively, with Adam optimizer on cross-entropy loss and learning rate <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math>. Each model has <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> layers, each layer with one attention head, embedding dimension <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=128</annotation></semantics></math> and an MLP with width <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4m</annotation></semantics></math> and GeLU activation. We use online training: at each training step, sample fresh new data to train. The batch size and training steps are <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32,400000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>400000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32,400000</annotation></semantics></math> respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We apply ANNA on all the <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> trained models. For the first layer, the number of hash tables <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen from <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{32,40,48,\ldots,96\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>96</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{32,40,48,\ldots,96\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen from <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,2,3,4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,2,3,4\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the second layer, the number of hash tables <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen from <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{4,8,12,\ldots,32\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{4,8,12,\ldots,32\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen from <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,2,3,4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,2,3,4\}</annotation></semantics></math>. When evaluating the test error, we compute the error on all the tokens. Note that this is different from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sanford et al. (2024c)</a></cite>, where they only compute the error on the tokens whose induction head exists to avoid overestimating the performance when <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is large and has a large fraction of null outputs. In our setting, <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math> which doesn’t have many null outputs, and it is important for the model to learn when to output the null token.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We found <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math> has the best performance, so we report it in <a href="#S5.F1.sf2" title="In Figure 1 ‣ 5.3 Experiments on Match2 and induction heads ‣ 5 ANNA-transformer for reasoning tasks ‣ Fast attention mechanisms: a tale of parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1(b)</span></a>. Again, the errors are averaged over <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> runs for each combinations and taken the minimum over <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>’s. One can see that <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32</annotation></semantics></math> hash tables in the first layer and <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> hash tables in the second layer already gives highly non-trivial performance: the error rate is <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.2</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> samples and each sample has <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> token predictions, while random guess would give <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.75" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.75</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.75</annotation></semantics></math> error rate. With more hash tables in the first layer, the error rate can go below <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</article>
